[Lemma lem:Evp of arXiv:2604.20094, 'Persistence and local extinction for superprocesses in random environments'] Let $T>0$. Suppose $f\in C_c^+  ({\mathbb R}^d)$
  	and $v$ is the unique solution to  (equation eq:PAM of the paper). Then for any $p\geqslant 2$,
  there is a constant $C = C(d,p,T,\|{\mathcal C}\|_\infty) > 0$ so that
  	\begin{equation}
	  \sup_{x\in {\mathbb R}^d, t\in[0, T]} {\mathbf E} [ |v (t, x) |^p ] \leqslant C \|f\|_\infty^p.
  	\end{equation}

[Lemma lem_multinomial of arXiv:2608.09105, 'Longest convex chains with i.i.d.\ points'] Fix $\varepsilon_1,\varepsilon_2>0$ and an integer $K\geqslant2$. Let $(M_1, M_2, \ldots, M_K)$ have the multinomial distribution with $m$ trials and probability parameters $(q_1, q_2, \ldots, q_K)$, where $q_k\geqslant\varepsilon_1$ for every $k$. 
Assume $m_1,\dots,m_K$ are nonnegative integers that sum to $m$, and
\eq{
|m_k - mq_k| \leqslant 1/\varepsilon_2 \quad \text{for every $k$.}
}
Then there is a constant $c = c(K,\varepsilon_1,\varepsilon_2) > 0$ not depending on $m,m_1,\dots,m_K$, such that 
\eq{
\mathbb{P}(M_1=m_1,\ldots,M_K=m_K) \geqslant \frac{c}{m^{(K-1)/2}}.
}

