body:
[Corollary 6 of arXiv:2607.20646, 'The Independence-Preserving Property and Planar Web Geometry'] Under the assumptions of \cref{thm:characterization}, assume moreover that three linearly independent Abelian relations 
    \begin{align}
        \big(\Phi_i^X(x), \Phi_i^Y(y), -\Phi_i^U(u), -\Phi_i^V(v)\big) \in \A(\W_F) \quad (i = 1, 2, 3)
    \end{align}
    are given.
    Then $F$ preserves the independence of $(\mu_X, \mu_Y, \mu_U, \mu_V)$ if and only if there exist real parameters $p$, $q$ and $r$ satisfying
    \begin{align}
        \mu_T(\dd t) \propto \exp\big( p \Phi_1^T(t) + q \Phi_2^T(t) + r \Phi_3^T(t) \big) \, \mu^0_T(\dd t)
    \end{align}
    for each $T\in\{X,Y,U,V\}$.

