[Lemma lem:cons-bound-gen of arXiv:2411.18749, 'A star is born: Explosive Crump--Mode--Jagers branching processes'] Under Assumption~(ass:star of the paper), there exist $\zeta < 1$ and $K = K(\zeta) > 0$ such that for all $a_1 > K(\zeta)$ and all integers $m\in \mathbb{N}$,
	\begin{equation}
	\sum_{\substack{a:|a| = m\\ a\text{ is $a_1$-conservative}}}\!\!\!\!\!\!\!\!\!\!\!\!\! \P{a \text{ has at least $a_1$ children before } \varnothing \text{ explodes}} \leq \zeta^{m-1} \mathcal{M}_{\lambda_{a_1}}(Y_{a_1})\mathcal{L}_{\lambda_{a_1}}(\mathcal{P}_{a_{1}}).
	\end{equation}

