[Corollary HalfSharp of arXiv:2504.18739, 'discrete analogues of second-order Riesz transforms'] For all $j,k=1,2,\ldots,d$, with $j\ne k$, we have
\begin{align}
    \|2\mathcal{R}^{(jk)}\|_{\ell^p\to\ell^p}\leq (p^\ast -1),\,\,\,\, 
    \|\mathcal{R}^{(kk)}-\mathcal{R}^{(jj)}\|_{\ell^p\to\ell^p}\leq (p^\ast -1),
\end{align} 
and when $k=j$, we have 
\begin{align} 
    \|\mathcal{R}^{(jj)}\|_{\ell^p\to\ell^p}\leq \gamma(p). 
\end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

