body:
[Theorem 33 of arXiv:2604.11682, 'Semilocalization for inhomogeneous random graphs'] There exists a constant $C_{\nu}> 0$ such that with $\nu$-high
  probability, for all $i \in [N]$, if $\lambda_{i}(A) > C_{\nu}\sqrt{\frac{\log N}{\log\log N}}$, then
  \begin{equation*}
    \left|\lambda_{i}(A) - \sqrt{D_{\pi(i)}}\right| \leq C_{\nu}\sqrt{\frac{\log N}{\log\log N}}\,.
  \end{equation*}
  or if $\lambda_{i}(A) < -C_{\nu}\sqrt{\frac{\log N}{\log\log N}}$, then
  \begin{equation*}
    \left|\lambda_{i}(A) + \sqrt{D_{\pi(N+1 - i)}}\right| \leq C_{\nu}\sqrt{\frac{\log N}{\log\log N}}\,.
  \end{equation*}

