[Theorem 19 of arXiv:2608.29152, 'Uniform Statistical Convergence of Empirical Sinkhorn Potentials\\ with Exponential and Po'] For a model satisfying Definition~\ref{def:tight-graph-model}, there exist constants $\eps_0, \eta_0>0$ and $C_0<\infty$ (dependent only on the finite model) such that for $0<\eps\le\eps_0$ and any $\delta\in(0,1)$, if 
\begin{equation}
 t_{n,\delta} := \sqrt{\frac{\log(2(I+J)/\delta)}{2n}} \le\eta_0,
\end{equation}
then with probability at least $1-\delta$, we have $d_\infty([\widehat f_{\eps,n}],[f_\eps]) \le C_0\eps \sqrt{\log(2(I+J)/\delta)/n}$.
This fixed-cost model maintains the $n^{-1/2}$ rate and features a favorable linear scaling with $\eps$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma k_0_all_nice of arXiv:2608.00399, 'The Heavy-tailed Frog Model'] Under the same assumptions and the choice of $\beta_0$ as in Lemma (lemma: recursion of the paper), if $\mathcal{G}_{k_0}$ denotes the event that all $m_{k_0}$-boxes are nice, then $\beta_1 \ge \beta_0$ implies
    \begin{align}
        \lim_{m \to \infty} \hat{\mathbb P}_{m,\beta_1}(\mathcal{G}_{k_0}^c) = 0.
    \end{align}

