[Theorem 35 (Anisotropic local law outside the spectrum) of arXiv:2608.29872, 'Local Laws and Outlier Eigenvalues for Spiked Separable Covariance Matrices'] Under the assumptions of Theorem \ref{local_law}, fix any constant $\epsilon>0$. Then, for any 
\begin{equation}
z\in S_{\mathrm{out}}(C_0,\epsilon):=\left\{z= E+ \ii\eta: \lambda_+ + n^{-2/3+\e} + n^{-1/3+\e}  q^2  \le E \le C_0 \lambda_+,  \eta\in [0,1]\right\},
\end{equation}
and any deterministic unit vectors $\uu, \vv \in \mathbb{C}^{p+n}$, the following anisotropic local law holds:
\begin{equation}
\begin{split}
\left| \langle \mathbf u, G(X,z) \mathbf v\rangle - \langle \mathbf u, \Pi (z)\mathbf v\rangle \right| & \prec q + \sqrt{\frac{\Im m_{2c}(z)}{n \eta}}  \asymp q + n^{-1/2}(\kappa+\eta)^{-1/4} .
\end{split}
\end{equation}

[Proposition 31 of arXiv:2602.14618, 'Finitary coding and Gaussian concentration\\ for random fields'] Let $Y=(Y_n)_{n\in\Z}$ be a renewal process with $\gcd\{k\ge1:f_k>0\}=1$. Then the following are equivalent:
\begin{enumerate}[label=\textup{(\arabic*)}]
\item $Y$ satisfies Gaussian concentration;
\item $\sum_{k\ge1}s^k f_k<\infty$ for some $s>1$;
\item $Y$ is a finitary process with exponentially decaying coding radius;
\item $Y$ is a finitary coding of an i.i.d.\ process.
\end{enumerate}

[Proposition 5 of arXiv:2603.25400, 'One-arm probabilities for the two-dimensional metric-graph and discrete Gaussian free fiel'] For all $h\in\R$ and  $0<\alpha<\beta<1$, there exists $c=c(h,\alpha,\beta)>0$ such that for all large $N$,
    \begin{equation}
            \mathbb P[ \text{there exists a circuit in $A_{\alpha N,\beta N}$ that surrounds $B_{\alpha N}$, on which $\varphi_N\ge h$} ]>c,
    \end{equation} 
and hence \begin{equation}
        \mathbb P[ B_{\alpha N}\stackrel{\varphi_N\le h}{\longleftrightarrow} \partial B_{\beta N}]<1-c.
    \end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

