{"artifact_digest":"sha256:eeb02eea07070c0381012c6e71b2157edd813abd82f04b7d5ef7cbc4301c7af0","artifact_path":"objects/sha256/ee/eeb02eea07070c0381012c6e71b2157edd813abd82f04b7d5ef7cbc4301c7af0.md","bundle_digest":"sha256:251e1eac7b2b954a692936bcdebcd492e59238b977a92bc816c47861baf93c23","bundle_entry_key":"2604-00635-lemma-45-ratefunctionlowerbound","bundle_id":"population.tex-extract-s3_004","claim_kind":"lemma","conditions":[],"domain":"probability theory","draft":"tex-extract-20260907/bundle_s3_004.json","evidence_ids":[],"logical_id":"math:harvest.arxiv.mathematics:arxiv-2604-00635-lemme-45-ratefunctionlowerbound","overlay_schema_version":1,"proof_text":"Paper's own proof, opening: From the inequality $\ln|x-y| \leq \ln(1+|x|) + \ln(1+|y|)$, and $\ln(1+x) \leq x$ for $x\geq 0$, we have

\begin{align*}

\Int{\mathbb{R}}{} \ln \max\Big\{ 0 ,  1+ \frac{2}{\ell} \Int{\mathbb{R}}{} \ln|x-y| \, \mathrm{d}\mu(y) \Big\} \, \mathrm{d}\mu(x) \, \leq  \,

\frac{4}{\ell} \Int{\mathbb{R}}{} \ln(1+|x|) \, \mathrm{d}\mu(x) \, .

\end{align*}

By \ref{potentialh2}, there exists $C^{\prime}>0$ such that $\frac{4}{\ell} \ln(1+|x|) \leq \frac{1}{2}V(x) + C^{\prime}$, which, all-in-all, entails the first lower bound.

For the second one, we use the non-negativity of the relative entropy $D(\mu \, \| \, \nu) $, or equivalently the Donsker--Varadhan variational formula.

