the edge that connects the starting point with $(0,-1,\dots, 0)$. For this choice of $i$ and $j$, we will prove that 
\begin{align}
&\left(\forall \omega\in\Omega\right) \quad \partial_{i,j}f(\omega)\geq 0 \quad\text{and} \\
&\left(\exists\hat\omega\in\Omega\right) \quad \partial_{i,j}f(\hat\omega)>0. \end{align} 
We will first prove 
(equation eqn|nonParasiteDirection01 of the paper). 
