{"artifact_digest":"sha256:b1c4330560e048ea163528cf9754b94c62b858e674794406037edad7559d7fce","artifact_path":"objects/sha256/b1/b1c4330560e048ea163528cf9754b94c62b858e674794406037edad7559d7fce.md","bundle_digest":"sha256:a969315ac9be5bfeec2f87e7c7b6f6658ea6d4dc22de9c62e05344c0b65a5e60","bundle_entry_key":"2512-07202-lemma-42-controlmoment","bundle_id":"population.tex-extract-s1_011","claim_kind":"lemma","conditions":[],"domain":"probability theory","draft":"tex-extract-20260907/bundle_s1_011.json","evidence_ids":[],"logical_id":"math:harvest.arxiv.mathematics:arxiv-2512-07202-lemma-42-controlmoment","overlay_schema_version":1,"proof_text":"Paper's own proof, opening: We assume without loss of generality that $s=0$ and aim at proving the following estimate:
\begin{equation}
\mathbb{E}\left[d(y_0, Y_t)^p\right] \leqslant C t^{pH}, \quad \text{for all } t \in [0, T],
\end{equation}
where the constant \( C \) depends only on \( H \), \( \mathcal{V} \), \( p \), and \(T\).
To this end, consider the rescaled rough differential equation
\begin{equation}
dZ_r = \varepsilon^{H} \sum_{i=1}^d V_i(Z_r) \, dB_r, \quad Z_0 = z_0 \in \mathbb{R}^N,
\end{equation}
