[Proposition 4 of arXiv:2511.00679, 'Stochastic solutions to abstract telegraph-type equations involving fractional dynamics'] Let $\{B(t):t\geq 0\}$ be the standard Brownian motion. We get that
\begin{align*}
\widehat\Phi_\frac{1}{2}(t,\xi) =\mathbb E \left[g(|B(t)|,\xi)\right],
\end{align*}
where 
$$g(t,\xi):=e^{-\lambda t}\left[\cosh(t\sqrt{\lambda^2-m(\xi)})+\frac{\lambda}{\sqrt{\lambda-m(\xi)}}\sinh(t\sqrt{\lambda^2-m(\xi)})\right].$$

