	In particular, $s_n \ge 3$ with probability tending to $1$ as $n \to \infty$. Hence throughout the rest of the proof, we may safely ignore the case $s_n \le 2$ and set any term that would be ill-defined for $s_n \le 2$ to some adequate placeholder value.

