[Theorem thm:budget-lower of arXiv:2608.20480, 'When Clean Data Hurts: Learning with Monotone \\ Corruptions Beyond Binary Classification'] Let $s=\min\{b,n\}$. For every $d\ge1$, there is a fixed countable multiclass
class $\mathcal{H}$ of DS dimension $d$ such that
\[
    R^{\mathrm{imp}}_{\mathrm{ad},b}(n;\mathcal{H})
    \ge
    c\min\!\left\{
        1,
        \frac{d\log(2+s/d)}{n}
    \right\}
\]
for a universal constant $c>0$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

