[Lm 17 of arXiv:2609.03836, 'Koszul Orlik--Solomon Algebras from Non-supersolvable Arrangements'] Let $M$ be a matroid and let $F$ be a modular flat of $M$ of positive rank.
        The rank of a flat $G$ of $\overline{T}_F(M)$ is given by
        \[
            \rk_{\overline{T}_F(M)} G = \begin{cases}
                \rk_M G & \text{if $F \cap G = \varnothing$}\\
                \rk_M G - \rk F +1& \text{if $F \subseteq G$}
            \end{cases}
        \]
        In particular, $\rk \overline{T}_F(M) = \rk M - \rk_M F + 1$.

[Lemma lem:pointwise of arXiv:2608.30166, 'Square Functions and Rectifiability\\ under Monotone Transformations of the Density'] Under the hypotheses of Theorem~(thm:main of the paper), for all $x\in\operatorname{supp}(\mu)$ and $r>0$,
\begin{equation}
\lambda^{-1}\,|\Delta_\mu(x,r)|
\;\le\;|\Delta^F_\mu(x,r)|
\;\le\;\lambda\,|\Delta_\mu(x,r)|.
\end{equation}

[Lemma lem:regularity_priori_estimate of arXiv:2606.31155, 'The well-posedness of stochastic Korteweg--de Vries equations revisited'] Let $s\geq 3$. Suppose $u_0\in H_x^s$ and $ J^s_xk\in L_x^\infty L_y^2$. For any fixed $ R,T>0$, let $u_R$ be the solution constructed in Proposition (localwellres of the paper).  Then for any stopping time $0\leq \sigma\leq \sigma_R^T(u_R)$ almost surely, we have 
		\begin{equation}
			\|u_R\|_{L_\omega^{p}L_{\sigma}^\infty L_x^2}\leq C(p,T,\|k\|_{L_x^\infty L_y^2})\|u_0\|_{L_x^2}, \quad \forall~2\leq p<\infty.
		\end{equation}

