[Lem Lem6.1-replacement of arXiv:2605.08052, 'Rapid phase ordering of Ising dynamics on $\mathbb Z^2$'] For $R$ and $\Delta$ as in Proposition~(prop:horizontal-splitting-beta-uniform of the paper), there exists $c_3,c_4$ and $s_0$ (independent of $\beta)$ such that if $\beta>\beta_0, s\ge s_0$ and $\ell \ge \beta e^{2\beta}$, and $\bar \alpha \ge \sqrt{C \log \ell}$ for $C$ large independent of $\beta$, then 
        \begin{align*}
            \pi_R^\eta (\partial \lambda_1 =\{x,y\}\,,\,\partial \lambda_2 = \{u,v\}) \le \ell^{c_3} e^{ - c_4 \bar \alpha^2}\,.
        \end{align*}

