[Definition def:monotonicity of arXiv:2605.10491, 'Zero-couplings of infinite measures with cyclically monotone support and multivariate regu'] A set $T \subset \reals^d\times\reals^d$ is cyclically monotone if,  for every integer $n \geqslant 1$ and all $(x_1,y_1),\ldots,(x_n,y_n) \in T$ with $y_{n+1} := y_1$, we have 
\begin{equation}

    \sum_{i=1}^n \langle{x_i,y_i}\rangle \geqslant \sum_{i=1}^n \inpr{x_i,y_{i+1}}.
\end{equation}
If (rel:cyclical_mononicity of the paper) holds for $n=2$, then $T$ is monotone.
The set $T$ is maximal (cyclically) monotone if it is not contained in a larger subset of $\reals^d\times\reals^d$ that is also (cyclically) monotone.

[Theorem 1 of arXiv:2511.09280, 'Random Walk conditioned to stay above a non-flat floor: curvature effects'] Let \(X, X_1,X_2,\dots\) be an i.i.d.\ family of \(\Z\)-valued, irreducible, aperiodic random variables satisfying~\eqref{eq:conditions_steps}. Let \(a_*,b_*\) be defined as in~\eqref{eq:dual_allowed_slopes}, and \(a_*<a<b<b_*\). Let \(h\in C^2([0,1])\) be a non-negative concave function with \(h''<0\), \(\mathrm{Image}(h')\subset H_X'([a,b])\), and \(h(0)=0\). Define
    \begin{equation*}
        h_n(k) = nh(k/n),\quad k=0,\dots, n.
    \end{equation*}
    Then, there are \(c_+\geq c_- >0, n_0\geq 1\) such that for any \(n\geq n_0\),
    \begin{equation*}
        e^{-c_+n^{1/3}}
        \leq
        e^{n\int_{0}^1 I(h'(s))ds} P\bigl(S\geq h_n, S_n = \lceil h_n(n)\rceil\bigr)
        \leq
        e^{-c_-n^{1/3}},
    \end{equation*}
    where \(S_0=0\), \(S_k=S_{k-1}+X_k\) and \(I(x) = \sup_{\lambda} \bigl(\lambda x - H(x)\bigr)\).

[Theorem thm:main of arXiv:2609.00668, 'Rigidity of Euclidean Minimal Hypersurfaces under Nonuniform Diagonal Dilations'] Let $n\ge3$, let $\Sigma\subset\mathbb R^n$ be a connected embedded $C^2$ hypersurface, and let $D_t$ have positive pair-sum-nonresonant weights. Put $N=\binom n2$. The following are equivalent:
\begin{enumerate}
\item $D_t\Sigma$ is minimal for every $t>0$;
\item $D_{t_1}\Sigma,\ldots,D_{t_N}\Sigma$ are minimal for some $N$ distinct positive numbers $t_1,\ldots,t_N$;
\item $\Sigma$ is a connected open subset of an affine hyperplane.
\end{enumerate}

[Lemma 12 of arXiv:2604.07697, 'Stochastic fractional heat equation with general rough noise'] For any $H\in (0,\frac12)$, there exists a constant  $c_H>0$ depending on $H$ such that for any $x\in\mathbb{R}$,
 \begin{equation}
 \int_{|y|>1}|y|^{2H-2} \left(1\wedge |x+y|^{2H-2}\right)dy\le c_H\left(1\wedge |x|^{2H-2}\right).
\end{equation}

