[Lemma 17 of arXiv:2604.15874, 'On Continuous Data Assimilation for a class of 2D and 3D stochastic non-Newtonian fluids o'] Let $\Grm\in \mathcal{L}_{\Qrm}(\Hbb)$ and let $\Rrm_{\h}$ satisfy \eqref{eqn-data-inter}. 
Let $\u$ and $\Urm$ be the solutions to the systems \eqref{STGF} and \eqref{STGF-CDA}, respectively. If $\kappa$ and $\h$ satisfy
\begin{equation}

0<\kappa \leq \frac{  \nu \varepsilon_0 }{c_0 \h^2 } 
\end{equation}
 where $c_0$ is the constant that appears in estimate \eqref{eqn-data-inter}, then $\Pbb$-a.s.  we have
\begin{align}
\left\| \u(t)-\Urm(t) \right\|_{2}^2 &\leq \left\|\u_0 - \Urm_0 \right\|_{2}^2 \cdot  \exp \left(-\kappa t + \displaystyle \frac{27[\mathrm{N}_d]^4}{16\lambda_1\nu^3\varepsilon_0^3} \int_{0}^t   \|\Arm(\u(s))\|_{4}^4 \drm s   \right), \qquad \text{ for any }t>0.
\end{align}

