[Lemma 16 of arXiv:2605.11877, 'Fluctuation analysis for a randomly perturbed dynamical system with state-dependent impuls'] For $\eps \in (0,1)$ small enough, $t \in [0,\sfT]$, we have
\begin{equation*}
\begin{aligned}
|R^\eps_{\lambda^\eps_t}-r(t)-\eps R^1_t| \cdot \ind_{\Omega\setminus G^\eps_\sfN} & \le   \left\{  e^{\lhp t/\alpha} (|r_0|+\sfK_b t) + e^{\lhp \Ren^\eps_t} \left(|r_0| + \sfK_b t + 2\eps(\Ren^\eps_t+1) \sup_{t \in [0,\sfT]}|W_t|\right) \right. \\ & \left. \qquad + \eps\,  2(\ren(t)+1) e^{(2\lhp/\alpha + \sfK_b e^{\lhp t/\alpha})t}  \sup_{[0, \sfT]} |W_t|\right\} \ind_{\Omega \setminus G^\eps_\sfN}
\end{aligned}
