	\end{enumerate}

[Lemma lem:far_term_bound_layer of arXiv:2607.04514, 'Boundary-layer asymptotics for Gaussian-smoothed singular measures'] Assume (ass:standing:measure of the paper) and~(ass:standing:chart of the paper) of (ass:standing of the paper).
  Fix \(A>0\). There exists \(\sigma_0>0\) such that
  \begin{equation*}
    \widetilde p_{{\mathrm{far}},\sigma}(a,x) = p_{{\mathrm{far}},\sigma}\bigl(y_\sigma(a,x)\bigr)
  \end{equation*}
  is well defined and satisfies \(\widetilde p_{{\mathrm{far}}, \sigma}\in \mathfrak E_r^2\) on
  \(\mathcal D_{A, \mathcal{K}_{\mathcal{S}},\sigma_0}\). Consequently, the normalized remainder
  \begin{equation*}
    \mathscr E_{\mathrm{far}}(a,x,\sigma)
    = (2\pi)^{d/2} \sigma^{k-2} \widetilde p_{{\mathrm{far}},\sigma}(a,x)
  \end{equation*}
  belongs to \(\mathfrak E_r^2\), and hence to \(\mathfrak B_r\), on the same parameter domain.

