[Corollary 25 of arXiv:2511.13404, 'Asymptotic stability and mean ergodicity of Feller processes on Polish spaces'] Let $\mathfrak{F}\subset B(\X)$ be such that $L_b(\X)\subset \mathfrak{F}$ and satisfy Hypothesis $\mathbf{(H_1)}$. Suppose that $\Phi$ is Ces\`{a}ro equicontinuous w.r.t $\mathfrak{F}$ on $\X$, then the following statements are equivalent: 
		\begin{itemize}
			\item [(\runum{1})] $\Phi$ is mean ergodic w.r.t $\mathfrak{F}$ with unique invariant measure $\mu$.
			\item[(\runum{2})]  There exists $z\in\X$ such that $\Phi$ satisfies the lower bound condition \eqref{eq:LBC_Q} at $z$.
		\end{itemize}

