[Definition 33 of arXiv:2606.11758, '2606.11758'] Let \(d\in\mathfrak D_{\xi,n}^{\mathrm{osc}}\), and recall that
\(m_+=m_{\xi,d,+}\).
Define
\[
    \widehat F_{\xi,d,n}^{\mathrm{pre,cap}}
    =
    \sum_{\ell=0}^{m_+-1}
    \mathbf 1_{\{\tau_n>\ell\}}
    \sum_{I\in\mathcal D_\ell([0,1])}
    \sum_{\substack{
        J\in\mathcal D_{\ell+1}([0,1])\\
        J\subset I
    }}
    X_{J,n}^{\mathrm{cap}}(\xi,d,\ell).
\]
For every integer \(L\ge1\), define
\[
    \widehat F_{\xi,d,n,L}^{\mathrm{post,cap}}
    =
    \sum_{\ell=m_+}^{L-1}
    \mathbf 1_{\{\tau_n>\ell\}}
    \sum_{I\in\mathcal D_\ell([0,1])}
    \sum_{\substack{
        J\in\mathcal D_{\ell+1}([0,1])\\
        J\subset I
    }}
    X_{J,n}^{\mathrm{cap}}(\xi,d,\ell),
\]
with the convention that the sum is \(0\) when \(L\le m_+\).

The corresponding unstopped arrays
\(F_{\xi,d,n}^{\mathrm{pre,cap}}\) and
\(F_{\xi,d,n,L}^{\mathrm{post,cap}}\) are obtained by removing the factors
\(\mathbf 1_{\{\tau_n>\ell\}}\). 
The same empty-sum convention is used for
\(F_{\xi,d,n,L}^{\mathrm{post,cap}}\).

Whenever the limit exists, set
\[
    F_{\xi,d,n}^{\mathrm{post,cap}}
    =
    \lim_{L\to\infty}F_{\xi,d,n,L}^{\mathrm{post,cap}}.
\]

[Definition Induced events of arXiv:2603.28936, 'Composition of random functions and word reconstruction'] For all $V_A^-,V_B^-,V_A^+,V_B^+\subseteq [n]$ and functions $\psi_a: V_A^+ \to V_A^-$ and $\psi_b: V_B^+ \to V_B^-$, we let $F(V_A^-,V_B^-,V_A^+,V_B^+,\psi_a,\psi_b)$ be the intersection of the following events (seen as events under the probability measure $\mathbb P$):
\begin{itemize}
\item[-] $\mathbf{a}(x)=\psi_a(x)$, for all $x\in V_A^+$;

\item[-] $\mathbf{b}(x)=\psi_b(x)$, for all $x\in V_B^+$;

\item[-]  $\mathbf{a}^{-1}(y)=\psi^{-1}_a(y)$, for all $y\in V_A^-$; and

\item[-]  $\mathbf{b}^{-1}(y)=\psi^{-1}_b(y)$, for all $y\in V_B^-$.
\end{itemize}
We denote $f_a^-=|V_A^-|$, $f_b^-=|V_B^-|$, $f_a^+=|V_A^+|$ and $f_b^+=|V_B^+|$. We call such an event an \emph{induced} event.  If the role of $V_A^-,V_B^-,V_A^+,V_B^+,\psi_a,\psi_b$ is irrelevant in the context, we write $F:= F(V_A^-,V_B^-,V_A^+,V_B^+,\psi_a,\psi_b)$ to keep the notation light. We also write $\textrm{Supp}(F):= V_A^-\cup V_B^-\cup V_A^+\cup V_B^+$ and $|F|:= |\textrm{Supp}(F)|$.

[Lemma 15 of arXiv:2607.27082, '2607.27082'] Let $X$ be a symmetric strictly $\alpha$-stable Lévy process with
$1<\alpha<2$ and Lévy measure \eqref{Levygene}. Then, for every
$0<\theta<1$,
\begin{equation}
\E[(\tau_1^+(X))^{-\theta}]<\infty.
\end{equation}

[Proposition prop:concentration of arXiv:2412.00279, 'Optimal local storage policy based on stochastic intensities and its large scale behavior'] Assume the above quantile is exact, in the sense that $E[U_{\theta_C}(0)] = C$. Take $C=cN$ with $0< c \leqslant 1$. Then for any $\varepsilon>0$:
  \begin{equation*}
    {\rm P}\left(\left| \frac{U_{\theta_C}(0)}{N} - c\right|>\varepsilon\right)\leqslant 2e^{-2N\varepsilon^2},
  \end{equation*}
  and therefore $U_{\theta_C}(0)/N\overset{{\rm P}}{\longrightarrow} c$ as $N\to\infty$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Corollary 22 of arXiv:2606.12720, 'On McDiarmid's Inequality under Dependence \\ via Approximate Tensorization of Entropy'] {Gaussian Hamming-Lipschitz Concentration}


    Let $X \sim \mathcal N(\mu, \Sigma)$ on $\R^n$ with $\Sigma \in \R^{n \times n}$. Assume $f : \R^n \to \R$ fulfills the bounded differences property with constants $c = (c_1,...,c_n)\T$. Then, with $\kappa^\star(\Sigma) := \eigmax{D^{1/2} \Sigma D^{1/2}}$ where $D := \diagonal{\Sigma\inv}$, 
    \begin{align*}
        \P\Parent{|f(X) - \E[f(X)]| \geq t} 
        \leq 2\exp\Parent{-\frac{2t^2}{\kappa^\star(\Sigma) \twonorm{c}^2}}
        \quad \text{for all $t > 0$}. 
    \end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

