[Definition 2 (Regular pre-grazing horizon) of arXiv:2608.16701, 'Order-Sensitive Fast-Synapse Limits in Sparse Excitatory--Inhibitory Threshold--Reset Netw'] A time $T>0$ is regular for the class solution when it is neither a firing
nor a release time of any class and there is $\gamma_T>0$ such that every
class firing time $s\in(0,T)$ is transversal:
\begin{equation}
 b_q(\theta_q,A_q(s-))+I(s)\ge\gamma_T.

\end{equation}
The first grazing time is the first threshold contact at which this lower
bound fails.

