[Lemma lem:Key2 of arXiv:2606.19313, 'Stability of Khintchine-type inequalities via log-monotonicity'] Let $r_k=r_k(X)$ for a random variable $X$. Let $\alpha=(\alpha_1, \alpha_2, \ldots, \alpha_n)$ be a weak partition of $q$ with length $\ell(\alpha)<q$. The following bounds hold.

\begin{enumerate}
\item If $(r_k)$ is log-concave, then $\prod_ir_{\alpha_i}\leq r_1^{q-2}r_2$;\\

\item If $(r_k)$ is log-convex, then $\prod_ir_{\alpha_i}\geq r_1^{q-2}r_2$.
\end{enumerate}

