[Definition def:JumpHKE of arXiv:2412.05030, 'Characterization of Subordinate Symmetric Markov Processes'] Let $\phi_j$ be a scale function.
  For a  regular Dirichlet form $(\mathcal{E},\mathcal{F})$ of pure-jump type, 
  we say that HK($\phi_j$) holds if there exists a heat kernel $p(t,x,y)$ of $(\mathcal{E},\mathcal{F})$
  and 
  there exist a properly exceptional set $\mathcal{N}$ and 
  constants $c_1 ,c_2 > 0$ such that
  for all $t > 0$ and $x,y \in M \backslash \mathcal{N}$,
  \begin{align}
    c_1 p^{(j)}(t,x,y) \le p(t,x,y) \le  c_2p^{(j)}(t,x,y).

  \end{align}
  Here, $p^{(j)}(t,x,y)$ is defined by
  \begin{equation}
    p^{(j)}(t,x,y) := \frac{1}{V(x,\phi_j^{-1}(t))} \wedge \frac{t}{V(x,d(x,y))\phi_j(d(x,y))}, \quad t > 0,x,y \in M.

  \end{equation}

[Corollary co-atomic decomposition of arXiv:2411.12623, 'Random signed measures'] Let $\xi$ be a random signed measure on $S$, then
	\begin{equation}
		\xi=\alpha_+-\alpha_-+\sum_{k\leq\kappa_+}\beta_{+,k}\delta_{\sigma_{+,k}}-\sum_{k\leq\kappa_-}\beta_{-,k}\delta_{\sigma_{-,k}}
	\end{equation}
	where $\alpha_+$ and $\alpha_-$ are diffuse random measures, $\kappa_+$ and $\kappa_-$ are random variables in $\mathbb{N}\cup\{0\}\cup\{\infty\}$, $\beta_{+,1},\beta_{-,1},\beta_{+,2},\beta_{-,2},...$ are positive random variables, and $\sigma_{+,1},\sigma_{-,1},\sigma_{+,2},\sigma_{-,2},...$ are almost surely distinct random points in $S$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

