[Lemma 51 of arXiv:2511.10535, 'Eigenvalues of Brownian Motions on $\mathrm{GL}(N,\mathbb{C})$'] For any $N \times N$ matrix $A$ with complex entries, we have that 
    \begin{equation}

        \sigma_{N-j}(A) \gtrsim \sqrt{\frac{j}{N}} \min_{i \in [m]} \text{\emph{dist}}(R_i, V_i)
    \end{equation}
    where $m = N - \lceil j/2 \rceil$, $R_i$ denotes the $i$th row of $A$, and $V_i = \text{\emph{span}}(R_{\ell}: \ell \neq i, \ell \leq m)$.

