[Theorem 9 of arXiv:2608.27500, 'Optimal Transport for Network Comparison: \\ A Review with Machine Learning Applications'] Let $G=(V,E)$ and $G'=(V,E')$ with $|V|=n$ be connected graphs. Then
    \begin{align*}
        \sum_{i=2}^n \bigg(\frac{1}{\sqrt{\lambda_i}}-\frac{1}{\sqrt{\lambda_i'}}\bigg)^2\leq BW(\mu,\nu)^2\leq \sum_{i=2}^n \bigg(\frac{1}{\sqrt{\lambda_{n-i+2}}}-\frac{1}{\sqrt{\lambda_i'}}\bigg)^2.
    \end{align*}

