[Lem 4 of arXiv:2607.22414, 'Asymptotic fluctuations in supercritical multi-type Crump--Mode--Jagers processes'] Assume that~\ref{assumpt:Malthusian alpha} holds and let $\varphi$ be a non-negative,
c\`adl\`ag characteristic satisfying~\ref{assumpt:dRimean}.
Then, for every $i \in [p]$, the function $t \mapsto e^{-\alpha t} \E^i[\cZ_t^\varphi]$ is bounded and
	\begin{equation*}
	e^{-\alpha t} \E^i[\cZ_t^\varphi] \xrightarrow{t\to\infty} \frac{\bv_i}{\beta} \int_\G e^{-\alpha s} \bu^\trans \E[\varphi(s)] \, \ell(\dd s).
	\end{equation*}
	In particular,
	\begin{equation}
	\E^i \bigg[ \sum_{u\in\Tree} \be_{\tau(u)}^\trans\varphi_u (t - S(u)) \bigg] \leq e^{\alpha t} C
	\end{equation}
	for some constant $C>0$ and any $t\in\G$.

