[Lemma 4 of arXiv:2506.17045, '\LARGE{On bivariate Archimax copulas: Level sets, mass distributions and related results}'] Let $\psi \in \mathbf{\Psi}$, $\varphi$ be its pseudo-inverse, $A\in\mathcal{A}$, $h_A$ be defined according to eq. \eqref{eq:fct_h} and $L$, $R$ be defined as in eq. \eqref{eq:definition_L_R}. Let $t \in (0,1)$, if $\psi$ is strict and $t \in [0,1)$ if  $\psi$ is non-strict. Then the following assertions hold: 
    \begin{itemize}
        \item[$(i)$] $\xi^t$ is a non-decreasing function;
    \item[$(ii)$] If $0<L<R$, then $\xi^t$ is strictly increasing on $\left(t,\psi\left(\frac{L\varphi(t)}{1-L}\right)\right)$ and $\xi^t(x) = \varphi(t)$ holds for every $x \in \left[\psi\left(\frac{L\varphi(t)}{1-L}\right),1\right)$;
