[Lemma lem:InducedTime of arXiv:2511.10630, 'Cutoff for generalised Bernoulli--Laplace urn models'] For all $\varepsilon > 0$ and $C > 0$, there exists some $C^\prime > 0$ such that for every $\theta > 0$, there exists some $\theta^\prime > 0$ such that
    \begin{equation*}
      \min_{\mathbf{x} \in \mathrm{Centre}(C)} \cP{S_{0, \theta^{\prime} n / \Phi_{\ast}^{(n)}; C^\prime} \geqslant \theta n / \Phi_{\ast}^{(n)}}{X_0=\mathbf{x}} \geqslant 1 - 4\varepsilon
    \end{equation*}
    for all $n$ sufficiently large.

