{"artifact_digest":"sha256:5040bd78c388b85ed6cef533d731ff306db08829b33a8e3f5cc86bb151f52af3","artifact_path":"objects/sha256/50/5040bd78c388b85ed6cef533d731ff306db08829b33a8e3f5cc86bb151f52af3.md","bundle_digest":"sha256:92f5c7494bd9ef5e35dc68bb9679420dabefaeb4fa07ce0be65b9fe2e862f25f","bundle_entry_key":"2608-25471-lemma-45-p-past-future","bundle_id":"population.tex-extract-s0_115","claim_kind":"lemma","conditions":[],"domain":"probability theory","draft":"tex-extract-v2-20260907/bundle_s0_115.json","evidence_ids":[],"logical_id":"math:harvest.arxiv.mathematics:arxiv-2608-25471-lem-45-p-past-future","overlay_schema_version":1,"proof_text":"Paper's own proof, opening: We claim that, for each $s \in [0,t]$,
  \begin{equation} 
    \mathbf{1}_{\left\{
      \Pi_s(B(X^1_s, r)) > L
    \right\}}
    \leq
    \frac{2}{L}
    \int_0^s
    \mathbf{1}_{B(X_s^1,r)}(X_u^1)
    \mathbf{1}_{\left\{
      \Pi_{(u,s]}(B(X^1_u, 2r)) \geq L/2
    \right\}}\,dC_u.
  \end{equation}
  Suppose that $\Pi_s(B(X^1_s,r)) > L$.
  Set 
  $s_0 \coloneqq \sup\left\{ u \in [0,s] \,\middle|\, \Pi_{(u,s]}(B(X^1_s,r)) \geq L/2 \right\}$.
  By the continuity of $\Pi_{(u,s]}(B(X^1_s,r))$ in $u$, we have $\Pi_{(s_0, s]}(B(X^1_s,r)) = L/2$.
  This, combined with $\Pi_s(B(X^1_s,r)) > L$, yields 
