[Proposition prop:fixed-interface-solution of arXiv:2608.30904, 'Entire monotone solutions of the anisotropic Allen--Cahn equation in dimension 5'] Let $f$ satisfy (equation eq:f-ball of the paper). For $\varepsilon>0$ sufficiently small,
there exists an invariant pair
\[
(v_{\varepsilon,f},\ell_{\varepsilon,f})
\in
\bigl(H^1(\mathbb R^4)\cap W^{2,2}_{\mathrm{loc}}(\mathbb R^4)\bigr)
\times H^{-1}_{\mathrm{loc}}(\Gamma)
\]
such that $v_{\varepsilon,f}$ is fiber-orthogonal and
\begin{equation}
N_{\varepsilon,\tau_*}(U_{\varepsilon,f}+v_{\varepsilon,f})
=
Z_{\varepsilon,f}\ell_{\varepsilon,f}
\end{equation}
in the weak sense. Moreover,
\begin{equation}
\|v_{\varepsilon,f}\|_{H^1_\varepsilon(\mathbb R^4)}
\le
C\|E^\perp_{\varepsilon,f}\|_{(H^1_\varepsilon(\mathbb R^4))^*}.
\end{equation}

