[Lemma lemma def barriers of arXiv:2411.14350, 'Randomized Geodesic Flow on Hyperbolic Groups'] Let $a\in G$ be such that $d_{{\mathcal G}}(a,o)\geq n$ and fix a point $\xi\in \partial \mathbb{H}^d$ and denote by $\alpha \in[0,\pi]$ the angle between the rays $[0,\xi)$ and $[0,\psi(a)]$. 
For fixed $n\in\mathbb{N},\varepsilon>0$, set $2M = \lfloor\alpha {\rm e} ^{\varepsilon n}\rfloor$ and let $I_{i} = [\frac{2i-1}{{\rm e} ^{\varepsilon n}},\frac{2i}{{\rm e} ^{\varepsilon n}}]$ for $i=1,..,M$.
Then there exist barriers $H_1,..H_M\subset G$ and $C_1>0$ such that
\begin{equation}
\sum_{a_{i} \in H_{i}}{\mathcal G}(a_i,a_{i+1})^2 \leq C_1 {\rm e} ^{-rn} {\mathcal G}(a_{i+1}, a_{i+1}^{n})^2
\end{equation}
for all $a_{i+1}\in H_{i+1}$ and where $a_{i+1}^{n}$ is a point on $[a_{i+1},0]$ such that $\lfloor d_{{\mathcal G}}(a^n_{i+1},o)\rfloor=n$.
In particular this also means that there exists $C_2>0$ such that
\begin{equation}
\sum_{a_{i} \in H_{i},a_{i+1} \in H_{i+1}}{\mathcal G}(a_i,a_{i+1})^2\leq C_2 {\rm e} ^{-rn}.
\end{equation}
These barriers can be defined as 
\begin{equation}
H_i = H(\alpha_i) = \bigcup_{\eta} \bigg\{x \in G: d_{{\mathcal G}}(x,o)\geq n \text{ and } d_{\mathbb{H}}(\psi(x),[0,\eta))<C_0\bigg\}
\end{equation}
where the union is over all $\eta\in \partial\mathbb{H}^d$ such that $\angle ([0,\eta),[0,\xi))=\alpha_i$,
for some choice $\alpha_i\in I_i$ for $i=1,..,M$ and for some $C_0>0$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

