[Problem 11 of arXiv:2608.25164, 'A time-fractional Kalman filter'] For every $t\in[0,T]$, find the unique
$\mathcal Y_t$-measurable random variable $\widehat X(t)\in L^2(\P)$ such that
\begin{align}
\E\big[|X(t)-\widehat X(t)|^2\big]
 =\inf_{Z\in L^2(\mathcal Y_t)}
   \E\big[|X(t)-Z|^2\big].                                    
\end{align}
Determine also the filtering error
\begin{align}
S(t)=\E\big[(X(t)-\widehat X(t))^2\big].
\end{align} (Stated as a problem by the paper; open unless the paper says otherwise.)

[Corollary cor:decomp of arXiv:2608.26765, 'Beyond Client Averaging: A Client-Independent Second-Order Stationary-Bias Component in St'] The $N^0\gamma^2$ coefficient in Equation~(equation eq:main-expansion of the paper) admits the canonical source-wise decomposition induced by the exact local second-moment identity in Equation~(equation eq:D2-exact of the paper):
\begin{align}
  B_{20}^{\mathrm{local}}(H)
  &:=-\frac{\tau\sigma^2}{4a}(H-1),                                  \\
  B_{20}^{\mathrm{ctrl}}(H)
  &:=-\frac{\tau\sigma^2}{12a}
  \frac{(H-1)(2H-1)}{H},                                               \\
  B_{20}^{\mathrm{SCAF}}(H)
  &:=B_{20}^{\mathrm{local}}(H)+B_{20}^{\mathrm{ctrl}}(H)
  =-\frac{\tau\sigma^2}{12a}
  \frac{(H-1)(5H-1)}{H}.                                               
\end{align}

[Lemma lem:key-lemma of arXiv:2411.03065, 'Growing conditioned BGW trees with\\ log-concave offspring distributions'] Let $n\geq 1$ and let $\mu_n$ and $\mu_{n+1}$ be two probability measures on $\{1,2,\dots,n\}$ and $\{1,2,\dots,n+1\}$ respectively.
	Assume that for $m=1,\dots, n$ we have
	\begin{align}
	\mu_{n+1}(m)\leq \mu_n(m)\geq \mu_{n+1}(m+1).
	\end{align}
	Then, there exists a coupling $(X_n,X_{n+1})$ of the probability measures $\mu_n$ and $\mu_{n+1}$ such that $X_{n+1}\in\{X_n,X_n+1\}$ almost surely.

