		We use Etemadi's truncation method. Define $Y_i := X_i \cdot I_{\{X_i \le i\}}$ and let $S_n^* := \sum_{i=1}^n Y_i$. Also, for a fixed $\alpha > 1$, we set $k_n := \lfloor \alpha^n \rfloor$.

		By Chebyshev's inequality (Lemma \ref{lem:2.2}) and Rosenthal's inequality for independent random variables under sublinear expectations (see \cite{Zhang16}), there exists a constant $c > 0$ such that:
