[Corollary cor:approximate_duality of arXiv:2509.10984, 'Weak Existence and Uniqueness for Super-Brownian Motion with Irregular Drift'] Let $(X_t)_{t\geq 0}$ be a solution to (equation eq:SPDE1 of the paper) with $X_0 \sim \eta \in \mathcal{P}_p(\mathcal{C}^+_{tem})$, $p>2$,  and let $a$ be defined as in (equation eq:def_d of the paper). Let $Y^n$ be as above, independent of $X$.
	Then there exists $T_0 >0$ , depending only on $a$ and $\langle \mu,1\rangle$, such that for each $X_0 \sim \eta \in \mathcal{P}_p(\mathcal{C}^+_{tem})$ satisfying (equation eq:cond_x_0 of the paper), we get
	\begin{equation*}
		\lim_{n \rightarrow \infty}\mathbb{E}[(-1)^{J^n_T}\exp\Big(-\langle Y_T^n, X_{0}\rangle-a \int_0^T\langle Y_s^n, 1 \rangle ds\Big)\Big] = \mathbb{E}[\exp(-\langle Y_0,X_T\rangle)],
	\end{equation*}
for all $T \leq T_0$.

