[Lemma 9 (Uniform pointwise peeling for indexed processes) of arXiv:2606.07931, 'Pointwise Complexity for Gaussian Fields:\\Upper Envelopes, Algorithmic Lower Bounds, and '] Let \(\{Z_x\}_{x\in T}\) be random variables, let \(d_0:T\to[0,R]\), and let \(\psi(r;\delta)\) be nondecreasing in \(r\) and nonincreasing in \(\delta\). Assume that for every fixed subset \(H\subseteq T\) and every \(\delta\in(0,1)\),
\begin{equation}
\mathbb P\!\left(\sup_{x\in H} Z_x\le \sup_{x\in H}\psi(d_0(x);\delta)\right)\ge 1-\delta.
\end{equation}
Then for every \(r_0>0\), with probability at least \(1-\delta\), uniformly over all \(x\in T\),
\begin{equation}
Z_x\le \psi\!\left(\max\{2d_0(x),r_0\};\frac{\delta}{1+\lceil\log_2^+(R/r_0)\rceil}\right),
\end{equation}
where \(\log_2^+(u)=\max\{\log_2 u,0\}\).

[Corollary 17 of arXiv:2608.17449, 'Spectral Simplicity and Joint Eigenvalue Densities\\ for a Non-Gaussian Brownian Time Chan'] For $\nu$-almost every $\eta$,
\begin{equation*}
 K(\eta,\mathcal G_\eta)=1.
\end{equation*}
For any such $\eta$ and any $s\in \mathcal G_\eta$, define
\begin{equation}
 d\widetilde M_{\eta,t}
 =\exp\!\left(\gamma\sum_{j=1}^N(t_j-s_j)f_j\right)
 dM_{\Phi(\eta,s)},
 \qquad t\in\R^N.

\end{equation}
Then
\begin{equation}
 \widetilde M_{\eta,t}=M_{\Phi(\eta,t)}
 \qquad(t\in \mathcal G_\eta),

\end{equation}
and $\widetilde M_{\eta,t}\in\mathcal M_*$ for every $t\in\R^N$.

[Lemma 7 (Uniform fourth moments near the zero shift) of arXiv:2608.07820, 'Linear Spectral Statistics for Entrywise-Transformed Spiked Wigner Matrices under Shifted '] Assume \eqref{eq:W5-package}.  There exist \(\delta_0>0\) and
\(C_4<\infty\) such that
\begin{equation}
 \sup_{|s|\le\delta_0}\E|Y_s|^4\le C_4.
\end{equation}
If \eqref{eq:W3-package} also holds, then \(\delta_0\) may be chosen so that
\begin{equation}
 \frac12\le v(s)\le\frac32,
 \qquad |s|\le\delta_0.
\end{equation}

[Proposition 20 (Second Ray--Knight isomorphism on a finite graph) of arXiv:2606.07931, 'Pointwise Complexity for Gaussian Fields:\\Upper Envelopes, Algorithmic Lower Bounds, and '] With the above normalization, under the product law of the walk and the independent fields \((\eta,\eta')\),
\begin{equation}
\Bigl(L_{\tau(t)}(x)+\tfrac12\eta_x^2\Bigr)_{x\in V}
\;\stackrel{d}{=}\;
\Bigl(\tfrac12(\eta_x'+\sqrt{2t})^2\Bigr)_{x\in V}.
\end{equation}
In particular, \(L_{\tau(t)}(v_0)=t\) almost surely. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Proposition prop:passage-limit of arXiv:2608.23545, 'Eulerian walkers on $\Z^2$ have range exponent $2/3$'] There is a deterministic continuous subadditive function
		$\mu:\mathbb R^2\to[0,\infty)$ such that $\mu(\theta x)=\theta\mu(x)$ for every
		$\theta\geq0$ and
