[Definition def:results:2measures of arXiv:2412.07710, 'An H-theorem for a conditional McKean-Vlasov process related to interacting diffusions on '] Let $\nu \in \mathcal{M}_{2, d}$. Define the \emph{lift map} to be the absolutely continuous measure $\psi_\nu^n \in  \mathcal{P}((\ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}^d)^{V_n})$ with density
\begin{equation}

    \psi_\nu^n\big(\mathbf{x}^{(n)}\big) := \prod_{v = -n+1}^{n-1} \nu(x_{v-1}, x_v, x_{v+1}) \prod_{v = -n}^{n-1} \frac{1}{\bar{\nu}(x_v, x_{v+1})}, \quad \mathbf{x}^{(n)} \in (\ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}^d)^{V_n}
\end{equation}
We note here that any empty products are interpreted as 1.

[Definition $E$-frame of arXiv:2608.30592, 'Infinite Matrix Operators and $E$-Frames in Hilbert Spaces'] [TAL]
The sequence $\mathcal{F}=
\lbrace f_{k}\rbrace_{k=1}^{\infty}$ is called an $E$-frame for $\mathcal{H}$ if there exist constants $0<A\leq B<\infty$ such that 
\begin{equation}
A\|f\|^{2}\leq\sum_{n=1}^{\infty}\left\vert\left<f,\left(E\mathcal{F}\right)_{n}\right>\right\vert^{2}\leq B\|f\|^{2}\qquad (f\in\mathcal{H}).
\end{equation}

[Theorem thm:Gibbs-deg-and-nondeg of arXiv:2603.01322, 'Gibbs conditioning, atypical consensus and splitting Gibbs measures on random regular grap'] Fix $\nu\in \P(\X)$. Let $h$ be an edge potential and fix $c\in (\k h_{\min},\k h_{\max})\setminus \mathsf{Range}(\k h)$  such that $c\neq \sref$. Then $U_n$ given $\Conset_n(h,\cc)$ lies in $\Gibbsdeg(\cc)$ asymptotically (in the sense of Definition (\oldref{def-condlim})), where
    \begin{align}
        \Gibbsdeg(\cc)\coloneqq \bigcup_{\X^{\downarrow}\subseteq \X}\bigcup_{\beta\in \R}\TISGM^{\exp (\beta h^\downarrow),\nu^\downarrow}_{T^\k}\bigcap 
        \left\{ \rho \in \P (\Tstar^\kappa[\X]): \pi_{\rho_1} \in \mathcal{B}_h(c)\right\},
    \end{align}  
   $h^\downarrow\coloneqq h\vert_{\X^\downarrow\times \X^\downarrow}:\X^\downarrow\times \X^\downarrow\rightarrow \R$ and $\nu^\downarrow=\nu\cpr{\cdot|\X^\downarrow}\in \P(\X^\downarrow)$, identified with its p.m.f. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma le:long_sum of arXiv:2606.16259, 'Super-Arrhenius relaxation of the triangular plaquette model in any dimension'] Let
\[
\lambda_d=\frac{d}{d+1}.
\]
Let \(X\subset\mathbb{Z}^d\) be a nonempty admissible set, and let \(\alpha\in X\). Then
\begin{equation}

\sum_{x\in X\setminus\{\alpha\}}
\lambda_d^{\rho(x,\alpha)-1}
\geqslant 2.
\end{equation}

