body:
[Prop 22 of arXiv:2606.08115, '2606.08115'] Let condition (C) be valid for a two-dimensional random walk $\left\{ \ov{S}_n\right\}$.
Then for any $\alpha > 0$ there exists a positive parameter $C = C(\alpha)$ such that for any sufficiently large $n$ and any
$\ov{x} \in K$:
\begin{equation}

\pr\left(\tau(\ov{x})> n, \ov{S}_n +\ov{x} \in K \backslash K_{n, \alpha}\right) \le \frac{C \ln^2n}{n^{p/2 + 1}} u\left(\ov{x}_0 + M \ov{x}\right),
\end{equation}
where
\begin{equation}

K_{n, \alpha}:= \left\{\ov{z} \in K: \mathrm{dist}\left(\ov{z}, \partial K\right) > \alpha \ln n\right\}.
\end{equation}

