in Proposition~\ref{prop:refined-coupling}.  The triangle inequality for the
RKHS norm gives
\begin{align*}
\KSD_\pi(\mu_t^N,\mu_t)
\le{}\frac1N\sum_{i=1}^N
 \|\xi_\pi(X_i^N(t))-\xi_\pi(\bar X_i(t))\|_{\mathcal H^d}
+\left\|\frac1N\sum_{i=1}^N
 \{\xi_\pi(\bar X_i(t))-S_\pi(\mu_t)\}\right\|_{\mathcal H^d}.
\end{align*}
By Lemma~\ref{lem:witness-lipschitz}, Cauchy--Schwarz, the uniform second
moment bound of $\mu_t$ which follows from Proposition~\ref{prop:subgaussian}, and Proposition~\ref{prop:refined-coupling}, the
expectation of the first term is at most
