[Theorem limCor of arXiv:2504.18739, 'discrete analogues of second-order Riesz transforms'] \begin{enumerate}[label=(\roman*), leftmargin=*]
\item 
For any bounded matrix-valued function $A$, 
\begin{equation}
    \|\mathcal{P}_Af\|_{\ell^p}\leq \|A\| (p^\ast -1)\|f\|_{\ell^p}.
\end{equation} 
\item 
For any bounded matrix-valued function $A$ satisfying the additional property~(equation Non-Symm of the paper) in Theorem~(thm:MartTrans of the paper),
\begin{equation}
    \|\mathcal{P}_Af\|_{\ell^p}\leq \|A\| C_{p, b, B}\|f\|_{\ell^p}.
\end{equation} 
In particular, if $b=0, B=1$, then $C_{p, 0, 1}=\gamma(p)$ as in~(equation ChoiAsym of the paper). 
\end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Theorem 13 of arXiv:2605.11279, 'Flocking with Multiple Types: Competition, Fluid Limits and Traveling Waves'] Suppose $\mu^1(\cdot)$ and $\mu^2(\cdot)$ are two elements of $\TTT$ that solve \eqref{originalMVE}, with initial conditions $\mu^1_0 = \mu^1(0)$ and $\mu^2_0 = \mu^2(0)$, respectively. For $i\in \{1,2\}$, define the type-wise (extended) cumulative distribution functions by $F_i^{\pm}(t,x) := \mu^{\pm,i}\bigparens{t, (-\infty, x]}$, where $\mu^{\pm,i}(t,A) := \mu^i\bigparens{t, A\times \{\pm\}}$ for $A\in \borel(\real)$. In addition, define 
    \begin{align*}
        \Delta_{\pm}(s,x) := F_1^{\pm}(s,x) - F_2^{\pm}(s,x),
    \end{align*}
    and let $D_{\pm}(t) := \sup_{x\in \real} \abs*{\Delta_{\pm}(s,x)}$. Also, let $D(t) := D_+(t) + D_-(t)$. Then there exists some constant $c > 0$, depending only on $v_+, v_-, \alpha^+, \alpha^-$, and $\lnorm*{\varphi}_{\infty}$, such that for any $t \geq 0$,
    \begin{align}

        D(t) \leq D(0) \cdot \e^{ct}.
    \end{align}
    In particular, if $\mu^1(0)=\mu^2(0)$, then $\mu^1(t)=\mu^2(t)$ for every $t\geq 0$.

