[Lemma lem:wellposed of arXiv:2607.24705, 'Derangetropy Operators'] Let $w \in \mathcal{W}$ and $f \in \mathcal{D}$. Then:
			(i) $\rho_{w}[f] \in \mathcal{D}$;
			(ii) if $w$ is positive on $(0,1)$ then
			$\operatorname{supp}\rho_{w}[f] = \operatorname{supp}f$, if in
			addition $w \in C^{k}$ and $f \in C^{k}$ then
			$\rho_{w}[f] \in C^{k}$, and if $w(1-z) = w(z)$ and $f$ is symmetric
			about $m$ then so is $\rho_{w}[f]$; in particular
			$\rho_{w}(\mathcal{D}_{+}) \subseteq \mathcal{D}_{+}$ for the three
			type kernels;
			(iii) $\|\rho_{w}[f]\|_{p} \le \|w\|_{\infty}\|f\|_{p}$ for
			$1 \le p \le \infty$, and for Lipschitz $w$,
			\begin{equation}
				\big\|\rho_{w}[f] - \rho_{w}[g]\big\|_{1}
				\;\le\; \Big(\|w\|_{\infty} + \tfrac12\,\mathrm{Lip}(w)\Big)
				\|f-g\|_{1}.

			\end{equation}

