[Lemma super_duality_lemma of arXiv:2504.04792, 'Uniqueness and Longtime Behavior of the Completely Positively Correlated Symbiotic Branchi'] Let $\dot{W}$ and $\dot{W_0}$ be two independent white noises on $\mathbb{R}_+ \times \mathbb{R}$. Let $\phi, \psi \in C_{\text{tem}}^+$. Define $(V_t)_{t \geq 0}$ and $(\Tilde{V}_t)_{t \geq 0}$ as the unique $C_{\text{tem}}^+$-valued solutions, of equation $((eq: dual of the paper))$, driven by $\dot{W}$ and $\dot{W_0}$, respectively, with initial conditions $V_0 = \phi$ and $\Tilde{V}_0 = \psi$. Then, for all $t \geq 0$:
\begin{equation}
\notag
    \mathbb{E}\left[e^{-\langle V_t, \psi \rangle}\right] = \mathbb{E}\left[ e^{-\langle \phi, \Tilde{V}_t \rangle} \right].
\end{equation}

