[Theorem thm:PTASEP-H4 of arXiv:2608.02772, 'Non-Abelian Hirota-Miwa Equations for the KPZ Universality Class'] The dressed observable satisfies the mixed diamond
equation
\begin{equation}
\begin{aligned}
&\bigl(q\mathcal{M}_{t+1, \mathbf{a}+\mathbf{1},
\mathbf{n}+\mathbf{1}}^{-1}
+ p\mathcal{M}_{t+1, \mathbf{a}+\mathbf{2},
\mathbf{n}}^{-1}\bigr)
\mathcal{M}_{t+2, \mathbf{a}+\mathbf{1},
\mathbf{n}+\mathbf{1}} \\
&\qquad - \mathcal{M}_{t, \mathbf{a}+\mathbf{1},
\mathbf{n}}^{-1}
\bigl(q\mathcal{M}_{t+1, \mathbf{a}+\mathbf{1},
\mathbf{n}}
+ p\mathcal{M}_{t+1, \mathbf{a},
\mathbf{n}+\mathbf{1}}\bigr) = 0,
\end{aligned}
\end{equation}
at every $(t, \mathbf{a}, \mathbf{n})$ with
$a_i < h_{n_i+1}(t+1) - 1$ for all~$i$.

[Prop strong inclusion of arXiv:2609.00436, 'A counterexample to the stable forking conjecture'] Let $Q \subseteq Q'$ be division rings with $Q$ a subring of $Q'$, and $M \subseteq M'$ with $M$ a left $Q$-module and $M'$ a left $Q'$-module, such that $M$ is a submodule of $M'$ with the induced $Q$-module structure. Then the following are equivalent:

    \begin{itemize}
        \item Every linearly independent set in $M$ over $Q$ remains linearly independent over $Q'$.

        \item Some basis for $M$ over $Q$ remains linearly independent over $Q'$.
    \end{itemize}

