[Lem 50 (Almost sure polynomial lower bound on $X_n$) of arXiv:2506.19123, 'The longest increasing subsequence of Brownian separable permutons'] There exists an almost surely positive random variable $M$ such that for all $n\geq 1$,
\begin{align*}
X_n \geq M n^{\frac{p}{2}} \quad \text{almost surely}.
\end{align*}

