[Theorem 13 (Asymptotics of the free energy) of arXiv:2601.16377, '2601.16377'] Consider an off-critical ensemble \eqref{eq_Hahn_cut_2} with fixed filling fractions. For any $\eps > 0$ and $\N$ larger than some $\N_0(\eps)$, we have
 \begin{equation}
 \Big|\log\Z_\N - \big(\I[\mu_1,\mu_2]\,\N^2 + (\hat{n}_1+\hat{n}_2)\N\log \N + \mathbbm{Rest}_1\,\N\big)\Big| < \eps,
 \end{equation}
 where $(\mu_1,\mu_2)$ is the equilibrium measure and  $\I[\mu_1,\mu_2]$ is the maximum of \eqref{eq_I_intro}, while $\mathbbm{Rest}_1$ is a twice differentiable function of the rescaled parameters $\hat{A},\hat{B},\hat{C},\hat{D},\hat{\mathfrak{t}},\hat{\mathfrak{h}},\hat{n}_1,\hat{n}_2$, which is bounded with $\N$ and whose first and second-order partial derivatives are bounded. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Proposition prop:slack of arXiv:2607.04620, 'The Exact Ville Identity\\ \large From the Absorbing Case to the General Law\\ with an App'] Under the hypotheses of (thm:general of the paper),
\begin{equation}
  \frac1b-\mathbb{P}(T_b<\infty)
  =\frac{O_b+b(D_b+R_b)}{b(b+O_b)}.

\end{equation}

