[Lemma 66 of arXiv:2605.10150, 'Rough path theory and an introduction to rough partial differential equations'] For each $p \geq 2$ there is a constant $C_p > 0$ such that
\begin{align*}
\bbe \big[ |\bbb_{s,t}|^p \big] \leq C_p |t-s|^p, \quad s,t \in [0,T].
\end{align*}

