{"artifact_digest":"sha256:e68972ba03de53923dd612652bb6884c0ebadbee99c6915a942358d7691bbdb3","artifact_path":"objects/sha256/e6/e68972ba03de53923dd612652bb6884c0ebadbee99c6915a942358d7691bbdb3.md","bundle_digest":"sha256:ef31c279540f07b385e45e4c24f5c194fc7920f9bf16129a9025ba54ed789300","bundle_entry_key":"2605-10150-lemma-65-lemma-q-bm-2","bundle_id":"population.tex-extract-s3_029","claim_kind":"lemma","conditions":[],"domain":"probability theory","draft":"tex-extract-20260907/bundle_s3_029.json","evidence_ids":[],"logical_id":"math:harvest.arxiv.mathematics:arxiv-2605-10150-lemma-65-lemma-q-bm-2","overlay_schema_version":1,"proof_text":"Paper's own proof, opening: By Lemma \ref{lemma-Burkholder} and H\"{o}lder's inequality we obtain
\begin{align*}
\bbe \big[ |\bbb_{s,t}|^p \big] &= \bbe \Bigg[ \bigg| \int_s^t B_{s,r} \otimes dB_r \bigg|^p \Bigg] \leq c_p \cdot \bbe \Bigg[ \bigg( \int_s^t | B_{s,r} |^2 dr \bigg)^{p/2} \Bigg]
\\ &\leq c_p \cdot \bbe \Bigg[ \bigg| \int_s^t | B_{s,r} |^p dr \bigg| \Bigg] \cdot |t-s|^{\frac{p}{2} - 1}
