[Definition def:moderate-selection of arXiv:2605.10617, 'Logarithmic scaling of selective sweep curves:\\ from tents to houses'] We will call $\varphi_N$ the {\em scaling factor}, and $b$ the {\em exponent} of the selection.
    We say that selection is \emph{moderate}
    if $b\in(0,1)$, {\em quasi-strong} if $b=0$ and $\varphi_N \to 0$, and {\em strong} if $\varphi_N\equiv 1$.

[Theorem thm:duality-regularized of arXiv:2605.14149, 'The mean-field limit of online stochastic vector balancing'] Let $p\in[2,\infty]$ and $\delta\in[0,\infty)$. Let $q=p/(p-1)$ denote the conjugate exponent, with $q=1$ when $p=\infty$. We have
\begin{align*}
    V_{p,\delta}^{\infty} =
    \sup
    \bigg\{
        {\mathbb E}[YB(1)] - \int_0^1\varphi_\delta\big(\big\|{\mathbb E}[Y\,|\,{\mathcal F}(t)]\big\|_{2}\big)\,dt
        :
        \begin{array}{c}
            Y:\Omega\to {\mathbb R} \mathrm{\ s.t.\ } \|Y\|_{q} \leq 1,\\
            \,
            {\mathbb E}|Y|\sqrt{\log(1+|Y|)}<\infty
        \end{array}
    \bigg\}
    \eqqcolon P_{q,\delta}.
\end{align*}
Moreover, there exists $\alpha\in\mathbb{A}$ such that the minimization problem $V_{p,\delta}^{\infty}$ is attained. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

