[Def-theorem def-bessel-p-drift of arXiv:2512.10625, 'Bessel and Dunkl processes with drift'] Let $R,R_+, W, C, k\ge0$ be given as above, and
 let $\lambda\in C$ be a ``drift vector''. Then the operator
   \begin{equation}
  L_k^\lambda f(x):= \frac{1}{2}\Delta f(x)  + \sum_{\alpha\in R_+}
k(\alpha)
\frac{\langle\nabla f(x),\alpha\rangle}{\langle\alpha ,x\rangle}+\frac{\langle \nabla_x J_k(x,\lambda), \nabla f(x)\rangle }{J_k(x,\lambda)}
   \end{equation}
   for $W$-invariant $f\in C^{(2)}(\mathbb R^N)$ is the generator of a Feller diffusion on $C$ with reflecting boundaries.
   These diffusions have the transition densities
   \begin{equation}
  K_t^{\lambda,k}(x,A)=\frac{|W|\cdot c_k\cdot e^{-\|\lambda\|^2 t/2}}{t^{\gamma+N/2}} \int_A e^{-(\|x\|^2+\|y\|^2)/(2t)}
 \frac{ J_k(\frac{x}{\sqrt{t}}, \frac{y}{\sqrt{t}}) \cdot J_k(y,\lambda)}{J_k(x,\lambda)}
\cdot w_k(y)\> dy
\end{equation}
for $t>0$, $x\in C$ and  Borel sets $A\subset  C$ with the weight $ w_k$ in (equation def-wk-A-general of the paper).
These diffusions  have modifications with continuous paths; they
will be called Bessel processes of type $R$ with multiplicity $k$ and drift $\lambda$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Corollary eq:theta-large of arXiv:2607.27613, 'Regularized Bulk Universality versus Bounded-Disorder Nonuniversality\\for Annealed Comple'] \label[corollary]{cor:theta-large}
As \(\left\lvertu\right\rvert\to\infty\),
\begin{equation}
 \theta_p(u)=-\frac{u^2}{2}+\log(p\left\lvertu\right\rvert)
 +\frac12-\frac12\log p+O(u^{-2}).
\end{equation}
In particular, \(\theta_p(u)=-u^2/2+O(\log\left\lvertu\right\rvert)\).

