[Theo 13 of arXiv:2512.02766, 'Fine-Graining and Continuous Space Scaling Limit of the $H^{2|2}$ Model on the Hierarchica'] Consider the \(H^{2|2}\)-model on the Dyson hierarchical lattice $\mathbb{X}$ with spectral dimension $d_s=2$ and inverse temperature $\overline{W}>0$. The Vertex Reinforced Jump Process on $\mathbb{X}$ is either almost surely recurrent or almost surely transcient. Furthermore,
\begin{itemize}
    \item If every vertex is visited infinitely often, then almost surely, $\forall x\in[0,1), \varphi_{x}=0$ and $\forall i\in \mathbb{X},\ \psi_{i}=0$;
    \item If every vertex is visited finitely often, then almost surely, $\forall x\in[0,1), \varphi_{x}>0$ and $\forall i\in \mathbb{X}, \psi_{i}>0$.
\end{itemize}

