Let t_N be the midpoint of the two means. Chebyshev gives mu(S_N<=t_N)<=1/D_N and nu(S_N>t_N)<=1/D_N. Choose increasing N_j with D_{N_j}>=2^j. Both error sums are finite. The first Borel-Cantelli lemma therefore makes the measurable event "S_{N_j}>t_{N_j} for all sufficiently large j" have mu-probability one and nu-probability zero. This is mutual singularity.","release_manifest_digest":"sha256:bd45047aedf298f05cedf2717c4f4d02edb0a54c37dbd48b782cc4c7d3259133","revision_digest":"sha256:c7a5eb729b2883223a37d98904cdfef2384f8ffa842ff96f6c5d9cfef0f87c91","source_id":"owner-work:w335:p0050-square-gap-singularity","source_revision":"author-checked-20261010-pending-independent-w347","statement_fidelity_reviewed":false,"supersedes":[],"trust_class":"curated_secondary","truth_status":"unverified"}

