[Dfn Definition:h-transform,general case with r0 of arXiv:2411.13765, 'Schr\"odinger Bridge Problem for Jump Diffusions'] As a result of Lemma (lem_martingale1_h(T)/h(0) of the paper),  
\begin{equation}
    \mathbf{P}^h:=\frac{\mathbbm{1}_{\left\{ X_0\in A_0 \right\}}}{r_0}\frac{h(T,X_T)}{h(0,X_0)}\mathbf{P}
\end{equation} 
defines a probability measure on $\Omega$, and $\mathbf{P}^h$ is called the \textup{$h$-transform} of $\mathbf{P}$.

