[Proposition 17 (First- and second-order Komatsu estimates) of arXiv:2608.17540, 'Pathwise stability for one-dimensional SDEs driven by Brownian motion and a symmetric stab'] There exists $C=C(\alpha,\varphi)>0$ such that, for all $x\in\R$, $\delta\ge2$, and $\eps\in(0,1)$,
\begin{align}
|u_{\delta,\eps}'(x)|
&\le C\left(|x|^{\alpha-2}\1_{\{|x|>2\eps\}}
+\frac{\delta}{\eps^{2-\alpha}\log\delta}\1_{\{|x|\le2\eps\}}\right), \\
|u_{\delta,\eps}'(x)|\,|x|
&\le C\left(|x|^{\alpha-1}+\frac{\delta}{\log\delta}\eps^{\alpha-1}\right), \\
|u_{\delta,\eps}''(x)|
&\le C\left(|x|^{\alpha-3}\1_{\{|x|>2\eps\}}
+\frac{\delta^2}{\eps^{3-\alpha}\log\delta}\1_{\{|x|\le2\eps\}}\right), \\
|u_{\delta,\eps}''(x)|x^2
&\le C\left(|x|^{\alpha-1}+\frac{\delta^2}{\log\delta}\eps^{\alpha-1}\right). 
\end{align}
In particular,
\begin{equation}
  \|u_{\delta,\eps}'\|_\infty\le C\frac{\delta}{\eps^{2-\alpha}\log\delta},
  \qquad
  \|u_{\delta,\eps}''\|_\infty\le C\frac{\delta^2}{\eps^{3-\alpha}\log\delta}.
\end{equation}

[Lemma 4 of arXiv:2606.22656, 'Fluctuations of Point Vortex Ensembles\\ at Small Negative Inverse Temperature'] For every $1\leq p<\infty$ there exists $C_p<\infty$ such that, for every $U\in\U(n)$,
\begin{equation}
    \int_{\T^n}
    \prod_{(i,j)\in E(U)}
    \bigl(1+|G(x_i-x_j)|\bigr)^p
    dx^n
    \leq C_p^n.
