body:
[Theorem 18 of arXiv:2605.14254, '2605.14254'] Let $X$ be a Feller process with arbitrary initial distribution, and fix any optional time $\tau$. Then these conditions are equivalent:
		\begin{enumerate}
			\item[(i)] $\tau$ is predictable;
			\item[(ii)] $\tau$ is accessible;
			\item[(iii)]$X_{\tau-}=X_\tau$ a.s. on $\{\tau<\infty\}$.
		\end{enumerate}

