[Definition 17 of arXiv:2605.30616, 'Brownian motion: the hyperbolic number setting'] Let $Z_{1}$ and $Z_{2}$ be two (not necessarily independent) $N(0,1)$
random variables defined on $(\Omega,\mathcal{C})$. The $\mathbb{H}$-valued random variable 
\begin{equation}
U\begin{pmatrix}Z_{1} & 0\\
0 & Z_{2}
\end{pmatrix}U,
\end{equation}
is called the $\mathbb{H}$-valued normal Gaussian variable associated
to $Z_{1}$ and $Z_{2}$.

