[Lemma lem:inserted_int of arXiv:2604.22528, 'Malliavin calculus for signatures with applications to finance'] Let $X = (X_t)_{t \in [0,T]}$ be an $\mathbb{R}^d$-valued continuous semimartingale. Then, for all ${\color{NavyBlue}{\mathbf{v_1}}}, {\color{NavyBlue}{\mathbf{v_2}}} \in V$ and $j \in \{1,\ldots,d\}$, 
    \begin{equation}
        \int_0^t \sigX[s]^{{\color{NavyBlue}{\mathbf{v_1}}}} \sigX[s,t]^{{\color{NavyBlue}{\mathbf{v_2}}}} \circ dX_s^j = \sigX[t]^{{\color{NavyBlue}{\mathbf{v_1 j v_2}}}}, \quad t \in [0,T].
    \end{equation}
    Consequently, for $\bm{\ell}_1, \bm{\ell}_2 \in \TA$,
    \begin{equation}
        \int_0^t \bracketsigX[s]{\bm{\ell}_1} \bracketsigX[s,t]{\bm{\ell}_2} \circ dX_s^j = \bracketsigX{\bm{\ell}_1 \otimes{\color{NavyBlue}{\mathbf{j}}}\otimes \bm{\ell}_2}.
    \end{equation}

