[Theorem main of arXiv:2412.06086, 'Zeros of conditional Gaussian analytic functions, random sub-unitary matrices and q-series'] Let $\varepsilon=-\log q$. If $(x,u)\in D=(0,1]\!\times \!(0,+\infty)\cup (1,+\infty)\! \times \![u_{-1}(x), +\infty)$
 then, in the scaling limit $\varepsilon\to  0^{+}$, $t \varepsilon=u>0$,
\begin{align}
F\left(x,\frac u \varepsilon ;q\right)= \displaystyle{\frac{\exp\left\{{\varepsilon^{-1} \big[\log x\log z_s+{\operatorname{Li}}_2(z_s)+u(1-z_s)-\pi^2/6\big]}\right\}}{\sqrt{1+(1-u)(1-z_s)/z_s}}} \left(1+O(\varepsilon)\right),
\end{align}
where
\begin{align}

z_s=
\begin{cases}
z_0(x,u) &  \text{if }  x\not=1 \lor (x=1\land u\ge 1) \\
z_{-1}(x,u) & \text{if }  x=1\land u\in (0,1)
\end{cases}
\end{align}

