body:
[Propo lem: c_k of arXiv:2606.15339, 'Uniform integrability of the distance to the nearest leaf in random trees'] Let $(\mathcal{T}_n)_{n\geq1}$ be a sequence of size-conditioned simply generated trees of type~I, II or~III, and set $c_k := \mathbf{P}(\partial(\hat{\mathcal{T}}) \geq k)$. Then $c_0 = c_1 = 1$ and, for every $k \geq 1$,
	\begin{align}
		c_k = \prod_{j=1}^{k-1} G'(F_j(1))\,.
	\end{align}
	For types~I and~II this admits the closed form
	\begin{align}
		c_k = {F_k'(1)}/{m}\,, \qquad \text{ for every } k \geq 1\,,
	\end{align}
	so that $c_k = F_k'(1)$ when $m = 1$ (type~I) and $c_k = F_k'(1)/m$ when $0 < m < 1$ (type~II). In type~III the limit $\hat{\mathcal{T}}$ is the infinite star, and hence $c_k = 1$, for any $k \leq 1$ and $c_k = 0$, for any $k \geq 2$.

[Proposition 2 (Information identity, ceiling, and comparison invariance) of arXiv:2609.02362, '\textbf{Farthest-cell triplet entropy: high-dimensional shell limits and hyperbolic curvat'] For every metric probability space,
\begin{equation}
  \log 3-\Htri(P,\metric)
  =I\{L_V(X);V\},

\end{equation}
and hence
\begin{equation}
  0\le \Htri(P,\metric)\le\log 3.
\end{equation}
Equality in the upper bound holds if and only if $q(V)=(1/3,1/3,1/3)$ almost surely. Moreover, the value is unchanged when every dissimilarity is transformed by a common strictly increasing function; in particular, it is invariant to global metric rescaling.

