body:
[Lemma lem:GramBound of arXiv:2410.23915, 'Asymptotic Bounds and Online Algorithms for Average-Case Matrix Discrepancy'] Let $A_1,\ldots,A_n \in \mathbb{R}^{m \times m}$ be symmetric matrices, and let $M$ denote the Gram matrix of $A_1,\ldots,A_n$ with respect to the Frobenius inner product. Then
        \begin{equation*}
            \sqrt{\frac{n}{m}\lambda_{\min}(M)} \leq \disc(A_1,\ldots,A_n) \leq \sqrt{n\lambda_{\max}(M)}.
        \end{equation*}

