[Theorem 8 (Gaussian comparison in Kolmogorov distance) of arXiv:2605.03100, 'Berry-Esseen bounds for multivariate martingale difference sequences in the Kolmogorov dis'] \cite[Theorem 2.3]{lopes2022CLT}
Let $\bm{Z} \sim \mathcal{N}(\bm{0},\bm{\Sigma})$ and $\bm{Z}' \sim \mathcal{N}(\bm{0},\bm{\Sigma}')$ where $\bm{\Sigma}$ and $\bm{\Sigma}'$ are $d \times d$ covariance matrices. Denote $\bm{D} = \mathsf{diag}\{\Sigma_{11},\Sigma_{22},...,\Sigma_{dd}\}$, and define
\begin{align*}
\Delta = \|\bm{D}^{-\frac{1}{2}}(\bm{\Sigma}' - \bm{\Sigma})\bm{D}^{-\frac{1}{2}}\|_{e,\infty}.
\end{align*}
Then the Kolmogorov distance between $\bm{Z}$ and $\bm{Z}'$ is bounded by
\begin{align*}
d_{\mathsf{K}}(\bm{Z},\bm{Z}') \lesssim \|\bm{D}^{\frac{1}{2}}\bm{\Sigma}^{-1}\bm{D}^{\frac{1}{2}}\| \Delta \log \frac{1}{\Delta}\log_+d.
\end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma lm:rem_bd of arXiv:2608.27828, 'Scaling limit of the 3D abelian Yang--Mills Langevin dynamics'] Under the same assumption as in lemma (lm:cubic_bd of the paper), one has
