$$
\lim_{m \rightarrow \infty} (X^m \in V) \xrightarrow[m \rightarrow \infty]{} \sup_{X \in \mathcal{T}(f)} P(X \in V).
$$
By lemma~\ref{conva.e.subseq}, the $1$st component of $(X^m)_m$, $(\pi_1 \circ X^m)_m \subset \mathcal{T}(f_1)$, has a subsequence which converges a.e.\ to some $X_1 \in \mathcal{T}(f_1)$. 
Successively repeating this for the other components leads to a standard diagonalization, from which one obtains a subsequence $(X^{m_l})_l \subset (X^m)_m$, such that
\begin{equation}
