  Then the \(\delta\)-structure on \(\widetilde{T} = \Spec(\widetilde{R})\) gives rise to a unique morphism \(\Psi_{\widetilde{R}} \colon \widetilde{R} \to W(R)\) of \(\delta\)-rings whose composition with the restriction morphism \(\res \colon W(R) \to R\) is equal to the canonical morphism \(\widetilde{R} \to \widetilde{R}/^L p \cong R\).
  This morphism induces a morphism
  \begin{equation*}
