[Prop 20 of arXiv:2606.17472, '2606.17472'] Let $B$ be a bounded closed interval. It holds that
\begin{align*}
\varphi_B(X_t)=\varphi_B(x)+\int_0^t\int_{\R\setminus \{0\}}\Big(\varphi_B(X_{s-}+y)-\varphi_B(X_{s-})\Big)\tilde{N}(ds,dy)+\int_B L_t^a \mu_B(da)
\end{align*}
for every $t$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Corollary 36 of arXiv:2609.03070, 'Variants of order semicontinuity in Banach lattices'] The following conditions are equivalent:
\item[(i)] $F$ is demicontinuous;
\item[(ii)] $F$ embeds isometrically as an order dense sublattice of a monotonically complete Banach lattice;
\item[(iii)] $F$ embeds isomorphically as a regular sublattice of a monotonically complete Banach lattice.\medskip

Moreover, the monotonically complete Banach lattice which contains $F$ isomorphically as an order dense sublattice is unique up to an isomorphism.

