body:
[Theorem 34 of arXiv:2511.07350, 'Decoupling of clusters in independent sets in a percolated hypercube'] {\cite[Theorem 3.6]{ross}}

Let $X_1, \dotsc, X_n$ be random variables with $\E[X_i^4] < \infty$,
$\E[X_i] = 0$, $\sigma^2 = \Var(\sum_{i=1}^n X_i)$, and define $\widetilde{W} = \sum_{i=1}^n X_i / \sigma$. 
Let the collection $(X_i, \dotsc, X_i)$ have dependency neighborhoods $N_i$,
$i=1,\dotsc,n$, with $D \coloneqq \max_{1 \leq i \leq n} |N_i|$.
Then
\begin{align}

    \mathrm{d_{Was}}(\tilde{W}, W) \lesssim
     \fr{D^2}{\sigma^3} \sum_{i=1}^n \E|X_i|^3
        + \fr{D^{3/2}}{\sigma^2} 
        \sqrt{\sum_{i=1}^n \E[X_i^4]},
\end{align}
where $W$ is a standard normal random variable and $\mathrm{d_{Was}}$ is the $1$-Wasserstein distance. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

