[Lem 20 (Control on the negative moments of $\sttm_k$) of arXiv:2506.19123, 'The longest increasing subsequence of Brownian separable permutons'] Let $0<\xi < \alpha$. Then we have
    \begin{equation}
        \Ec{\sttm_k^{-\xi}} = k^{-\frac{\xi}{\alpha}+o(1)} \qquad \text{as } k \to \infty.
    \end{equation} 
    In particular, we have
    \begin{equation}
        \Ec{\sttm_k^{-1/2}} = k^{-\frac{1}{2\alpha}+o(1)} \qquad \mbox{ and } \qquad \Ec{\sttm_k^{-3/2}} = o \left( \frac{1}{k} \Ec{\sttm_k^{-1/2}} \right) \qquad \text{as } k \to \infty.
    \end{equation}

