body:
[Lemma 12 of arXiv:2608.21905, '\bf Ruin theory incorporating MIPP-type jumps'] For the MIPP $V_t^{(n)}$, the following identity holds:
\begin{equation}
\begin{split}
 E\bigl[V_t^{(n)}z^{V_t^{(n)}}\bigr]
 =\lambda^n t\bigl(g_n^{\circ}(z)\bigr)^t\prod_{i=0}^{n-1}g_i^{\circ}(z),
\end{split}
\end{equation}
where $g_0^{\circ}(z)=z$ and $g_1^{\circ}(z)=g(z)=e^{-\lambda+\lambda z}$.

metadata_json:
{"artifact_digest":"sha256:a6a36e84b66be2eda3ec7a5d5430043db5af9e5e271beb18e368c16832309117","artifact_path":"objects/sha256/a6/a6a36e84b66be2eda3ec7a5d5430043db5af9e5e271beb18e368c16832309117.md","bundle_digest":"sha256:13547a0bdce918b1149774ab7a1c4db56ec5cc2b004a0dd27b3c3d13eed5c6f2","bundle_entry_key":"2608-21905-lemma-11-lem-exp","bundle_id":"population.tex-extract-s3_104","claim_kind":"lemma","conditions":[],"domain":"probability theory","draft":"tex-extract-20260907/bundle_s3_104.json","evidence_ids":[],"logical_id":"math:harvest.arxiv.mathematics:arxiv-2608-21905-lemma-11-lem-exp","overlay_schema_version":1,"proof_text":"Paper's own proof, opening: The proof is by induction on $n$. For $n=1$ we obtain
\begin{equation*}
\begin{split}
 E[N_tz^{N_t}]
 &=\sum_{k=0}^{+\infty}P(N_t=k)\,kz^k
 =e^{-\lambda t}\sum_{k=0}^{+\infty}\frac{(\lambda t)^k}{k!}kz^k\\
 &=\lambda t z\, e^{-\lambda t}\sum_{k=0}^{+\infty}\frac{(\lambda t z)^k}{k!}
 =\lambda t z\, e^{-\lambda t+\lambda t z}
 =\lambda t z\,(g(z))^t,
\end{split}
\end{equation*}
which coincides with (\ref{lap_mix}) in the case $n=1$. Now assume the identity holds for some $n$. We then treat the case $n+1$:
\begin{equation*}
\begin{split}
