[Theorem 4 of arXiv:2604.27485, 'On large deviation principles for general random processes \footnote{Research supported by'] In the general case, the l.d.p.\ always implies the l.l.d.p. Con\-versely, let the following condition be met: for any $N>0$ there exists a $v>0$ such that 
\begin{equation}

\limsup_{T\to\infty} \frac1T \ln \mathbf{P} (|z(T)|>v) \le -N.
\end{equation}
Then the  l.l.d.p.\ implies the l.d.p. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Proposition 10 of arXiv:2604.05910, '\textbf{Well-posedness and Hurst parameter estimation for fluid equations driven by fracti'] There exists a constant $C=C\left( t\right) $ independent of $n$ and $H$ such
that 
\begin{equation}
\mathbb{E}\left[ \left( \left( \frac{1}{n}\right) ^{1-2H}\sum_{j\in \mathcal{A}
_{t}^{n}}\left( W_{t_{j+1}}^{H}-W_{t_{j}}^{H}\right) ^{2}-t\right) ^{2}
\right] \leq \frac{C}{n^{4-4H}}.  
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Proposition error4d of arXiv:2605.12777, 'Mesoscopic Rates of Convergence for Complex Wishart Matrices at the Leftmost Spectrum Edge'] Let $R'_{n-1,N}(s)$ and $R'_{n,N-1}(s)$ be the error terms given in (equation a4D of the paper), then
    \begin{equation*}
        N^{\frac{2}{3}}|R'_{n-1,N}(s)||Ai'(s)|,~N^{\frac{2}{3}}|R'_{n,N-1}(s)||Ai'(s)|\le C(s_0,\gamma)e^{-\frac{s}{2}}
    \end{equation*}
    for any $s\in\left[s_0,N^\frac{1}{6}\right]$ when $N$ is large.

