[Thm network-archeology-root-finding of arXiv:2607.21428, 'Subcritical percolation and network archaeology on random recursive tree substrate network'] Fix \(\gl>0\) and choose \(q\) satisfying (equation eq:arch-q-range of the paper). For every
		\(\varepsilon>0\), there exist finite \(K=K(\varepsilon,q,\gl)\) and
		\(L=L(\varepsilon,q,\gl)\) such that the algorithm
		(equation eq:arch-algorithm of the paper) satisfies
		\begin{equation}

			\liminf_{n\to\infty}
			\mathbb P\{1\in \mathcal{H}_{K,L}(G_n^\circ)\}
			\geqslant 1-\varepsilon .
		\end{equation}
		Thus the original unlabeled observation \(G_n^\circ\), before the auxiliary
		percolation, admits a root confidence set whose size is deterministically
		bounded by \(K(\varepsilon,q,\gl)L(\varepsilon,q,\gl)\). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma 38 of arXiv:2605.10150, 'Rough path theory and an introduction to rough partial differential equations'] Let $f_0 \in \Lip([0,T] \times W, \bar{W})$ be arbitrary. Then we have
\begin{align}
| f_0(t,y) - f_0(t,z) | &\leq \| f_0 \|_{\Lip} |y-z|, \quad \text{$y,z \in W$ and $t \in [0,T]$,}
\\  |f_0(t,y)| &\leq \| f_0 \|_{\Lip} (1 + |y|), \quad \text{$y \in W$ and $t \in [0,T]$.}
\end{align}

