 The \emph{Jacobiator}\index{Jacobiator}  is the $\mathbb{R}$-trilinear
map $J_{A_U}:\Gamma(A_{U})^{3}\to\Gamma(A_{ U})$ defined, for any open set $U$ in $M$ and any $\left( \mathfrak{u}_{1}, \mathfrak{u}_{2}, \mathfrak{u}_{3} \right) \in \Gamma(A_{U})^3$ by
\[
J_{A_{U}}( \mathfrak{u}_{1}, \mathfrak{u}_{2}, \mathfrak{u}_{3}
)=\LB[ \mathfrak{u}_{1},\LB[ \mathfrak{u}_{2}, \mathfrak{u}_{3}]_A]_{A}+\LB[ \mathfrak{u}_{2},\LB[ \mathfrak{u}_{3}, \mathfrak{u}_{1}]_{A}]_{A}+\LB[ \mathfrak{u}_{3},\LB[ \mathfrak{u}_{1}, \mathfrak{u}_{2}]_{A}]_{A}
\]

