[Corollary cor:eprocess-retention of arXiv:2608.20295, 'Physical-Support Confidence Sets for Highly Coherent Dictionaries'] Suppose the candidate laws, data split, proposal construction, and evaluation
checkpoints are fixed before held-out evaluation.
If a candidate is rejected only after
Equation~(equation eq:candidate-rejection-threshold of the paper), then for every data-generating
candidate $e_\star\in\mathcal B$,
\begin{equation}
    \mathbb P_{e_\star}
    \left\{
        e_\star
        \text{ is ever rejected}
    \right\}
    \le
    \alpha_{\mathcal B}.

\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Definition 5 (Inverted Dirichlet distribution) of arXiv:2605.21424, 'A dice game, a multinomial walk, and the inverted Dirichlet distribution'] \hfill\\
Let \(m\ge 2\) be an integer and \(n_1,\ldots,n_m\in (0,\infty)\).
A random vector $(X_2,\dotsc,X_m)$ with values in \([0,\infty)^{m-1}\) has an \emph{inverted Dirichlet distribution} with parameter set $(n_2,\dotsc,n_m;n_1,\lambda)$, denoted by $(X_2,\dotsc,X_m)\sim \operatorname{ID}(n_2,\dotsc,n_m;n_1,\lambda)$, if it has the joint density
\begin{align*}
(s_2,\dotsc,s_m)\mapsto\frac{1}{\Beta(n_1,\dotsc,n_m)}\frac{\lambda^{n_1}\prod_{k=2}^m s_k^{n_{k}-1}}{\Big(\lambda+\sum_{k=2}^m s_k\Big)^{\sum_{k=1}^m n_k}}
\end{align*}
on $[0,\infty)^{m-1}$.
Here $\Beta(n_1,\dotsc,n_m):=\frac{\prod_{k=1}^m \Gamma(n_k)}{\Gamma\big(\sum_{k=1}^m n_k\big)}$ is the multivariate Euler beta function.

In the case where \(\lambda=1\) we simply write \((X_2,\dotsc,X_m)\sim\operatorname{ID}(n_2,\dotsc,n_m;n_1)\).

[Lemma le:laplace-tail-bound of arXiv:2608.30382, 'Convergence rates for the RMSprop optimizer with full control of the hyperparameters'] Let $ c, q \in (0,\infty) $, $ \beta \in (0, 1) $, $ n \in {\mathbb N} $.
Let $ V_n^* $ be a nonnegative random variable which satisfies for all $\lambda \in[0,\infty)$ that
\bas{

  -
  \ln \mathbb{E}\bigl[
    e^{-\lambda V_n^*}
  \bigr]
  \ge \sum_{ k = 1 }^n \min\Bigl\{ q, c \frac{1-\beta}{1-\beta^n} \beta^{n-k} \lambda \Bigr\} .
}
Then 
\bas{
  {\mathbb P}\bigl( V_n^* \le c / 2 \bigr)
  \le
  \exp\Bigl(
    - \frac q2 \, \frac{ 1 - \beta^n }{ 1 - \beta }
  \Bigr) .
}

