[Proposition 15 of arXiv:2607.02108, 'A Two-Color Lift of the Shifted \texorpdfstring{$t$}{t}-Schur Measure'] In the rectangular specialization,
\begin{equation}
        Z_q
        =\left(\frac{1+xy}{1-xy}\right)^L
        \left(\frac{1+qxy}{1-qxy}\right)^L.
\end{equation}
The two time symbols are
\begin{equation}
        J_1(z)
        =\left(\frac{1+yz}{1-yz}\right)^N
        \left(\frac{z+qx}{z-qx}\right)^M,
\end{equation}
\begin{equation}
        J_2(z)
        =J_1(z)
        \left(\frac{z+x}{z-x}\right)^M.
\end{equation}

[Theorem 11 (Finite block theorem) of arXiv:2608.25925, '\textbf{Jump Closure and Limit Uniformization\\in the Ideal Completion of the Turing Degre'] For every integer $m\geq1$, the closure ordinal of $\Theta_m$, starting from $\down\mathbf0$, is
\[
\omega m,
\]
and its least fixed point is
