[Proposizione 5 of arXiv:2506.11937, 'Random rotational invariance of integration by parts formulas within a Bismut-type approac'] Let $ B: M  \rightarrow SO(m)$ be a smooth function and let $ X$ be a weak solution to $SDE_{\mu,\sigma}$ driven by $W$. Let $ W'$ be the solution to \begin{equation*} d W'_t = B(X_t,t) d W_t, \end{equation*} then $ X$ is also a weak solution to $ SDE_{\mu',\sigma'}$ driven by $W'$, with 
\begin{equation*} \mu' = \mu; \ \ \ \  \sigma'= \sigma  B^{-1}. 
\end{equation*}

