[Corollary cor:LLN of arXiv:2606.09386, 'High-degree vertices in uniform recursive directed acyclic graphs with freezing'] Fix $m\in\mathbb{N}$,  a choice sequence $\mathbf x$ such that Assumption~$\hyperref[ass:A]{\mathbf{x}}$ is satisfied for some $\varepsilon\in(0,1/((m+1)\log \theta))$ in  Part~(item:hI of the paper) and some $\eta\in(0,1/((m+1)\log\theta))$ in Part~(item:Jn of the paper). Define for $i\in\mathbb{N}_0$,        \begin{align}
N^{(n)}_i &\coloneq  |\{v \in \mathbb A_n \colon \deg_n(v) =  i\}|, &&\,N^{(n)}_{\geq i} \coloneq  |\{v \in \mathbb A_n \colon \deg_n(v) \geq   i\}|,
\intertext{and}
M^{(n)}_i &\coloneq  |\{v \in \mathbb F_n \colon \deg_n(v) =    i\}|, 
&&M^{(n)}_{\geq i} \coloneq  |\{v \in \mathbb F_n \colon \deg_n(v) \geq    i\}|.
