[Cor 15 of arXiv:2609.03713, 'A Sharp Mass Threshold for Boundedness in a Critical Quasilinear Chemotaxis Model with Ind'] Let $a>0$ and consider a sequence $(u_l)_{l\ge 1}$ in $\Sigma_a$ such that $\lambda_l^d:=\|u_l\|_\infty\to \infty$.
Then there exists a constant $\kappa>0$ depending on $d$, $a$, and $R$ such that
\begin{equation}
	\lim_{l\to\infty} \left(\max_{r\in [\kappa/\lambda_l,R/2] }u_l(r)\right)=0\,.
\end{equation}

