body:
[Lemma 34 of arXiv:2506.09592, 'Extremal process of the local time of simple\\random walk on a regular tree'] There exists~$\tilde c>0$ such that for all $n\ge1$, all $\gamma\colon\{0,\dots,n\}\to[0,\infty)$ and all $s\ge u\ge0$,
\begin{equation}

\begin{aligned}
Q_{n,s,u}\Biggl(\biggl(\,\bigcap_{j=k}^{n-k'}\Bigl\{h(x_j)\le&\frac {n-j}n\wt m_n+s-\gamma(j)\Bigr\}\biggr)^\cc\,\cap\,\bigcap_{i=1}^n\Bigl\{h(x_i)\le\frac {n-i}n\wt m_n+s+\gamma(i)\Bigr\}\Biggr)
\\
&\le
\tilde c\frac{(1+s-u)(1+s)}n\sum_{\ell=k}^{n-k'}\frac{n^{3/2}}{[\ell(n-\ell)]^{3/2}}\,\gamma(\ell)^5
\end{aligned}
\end{equation}
for any~$k,k'=1,\dots,\lfloor n/2\rfloor$ such that $\gamma(i)\ge1$ for all~$i=k,\dots,n-k'$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lem 10 of arXiv:2609.01101, '2609.01101'] For $N\ge1$ and arbitrary complex numbers $d_n$,
\begin{equation}
\int_{-\infty}^{\infty}
\left|\sum_{n\le N}d_n n^{-it}\right|^2w_T(t)\,dt
=\frac{\sqrt\pi T}{2}\sum_{n\le N}|d_n|^2
+O\left(N\log(2N)\sum_{n\le N}|d_n|^2\right).
\end{equation}
The absolute constant in the error does not depend on the $d_n$.

