[Lemma 7 of arXiv:2511.06196, 'Central limit theorem for high temperature spin models via martingale embedding'] Let $p_d$, $d=0,1,2,\dots$, denote the probability mass function of $D_\infty$. We have, for some $d_1$ depending only on $\alpha$ and any $d_2\geq 1$,
\be{
\frac{p_{d_1+d_2}}{p_{d_1}}\leq C c^{d_2},
}
where $0<c<1$ depends only on $\alpha$.

