	\mspace{2mu}
 r_G}$ induce mutually inverse equivalences 
        $\smash{\textup{pic}(\Sp_G^{\otimes})\simeq \textup{pic}(\Sp_\text{$G$-gl}^{\otimes})}$ for all compact Lie groups $G$.  
        In particular, $i$ restricts to an equivalence $\smash{\textup{pic}({\mathpalette\ulhelper{\mathfrak S\kern-.5pt\mathfrak p}}\hbox{\rule[-2pt]{0pt}{0pt}}^{\otimes})\xrightarrow{\;\smash{\raisebox{-0.25ex}{\ensuremath{\scriptstyle\sim}}}\;} \textup{pic}({\mathpalette\ulhelper{\mathfrak S\kern-.5pt\mathfrak p}}\hbox{\rule[-2pt]{0pt}{0pt}}_{\textup{gl}}^{\otimes})}$, so that ${\mathpalette\ulhelper{\mathfrak J}}\hbox{\rule[-2pt]{0pt}{0pt}}_\textup{gl}^\otimes$ factors uniquely through ${\mathpalette\ulhelper{\mathfrak S\kern-.5pt\mathfrak p}}\hbox{\rule[-2pt]{0pt}{0pt}}^\otimes$ as claimed.
    \end{proof} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Theorem thm:results:uniqueRegime of arXiv:2412.07710, 'An H-theorem for a conditional McKean-Vlasov process related to interacting diffusions on '] Suppose $(U, W)$ satisfy Assumption (as:results:fixedPoint of the paper) and Assumption (as:results:LSI of the paper). Then there exists a unique Cayley fixed point $\pi \in \tilde{\mathcal{M}}_{2, d}$ and we have $\mathbb H_2^* = \mathbb H_2(\pi)$. In other words, for $\mathcal{Z}^n$ as in (equation eq:results:gibbsPFN of the paper), we have
\begin{equation*}
    \lim_{n \rightarrow \infty} \frac{1}{2n+1} \log \mathcal{Z}^n = \mathbb H_2(\pi).
\end{equation*}
Furthermore, we have \begin{equation}
        \mathbb H_2(\nu) - \mathbb H_2(\pi) = \mathcal{H}(\nu|\pi) - \mathcal{H}(\bar{\nu}|\bar{\pi}), \quad \nu \in \mathcal{Q}_{2, d}.

    \end{equation}
Moreover, if there exists a solution to the 2-MLFE with potentials $(U, W)$ and initial distribution $\pi$, then $\pi$ is the unique stationary distribution of the 2-MLFE in the sense of Definition (def:results:stationary of the paper). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Corollary cor:srd-L^2 of arXiv:2506.17168, '{\bf Scaling limits for sample autocovariance operators of Hilbert space-valued linear pro'] Let $\{X_n\}_{n \in \mathbb Z}$ be an $L^2(\mathbb{Y})$-valued process (equation eq:XninL2 of the paper) and consider its autocovariance operators $( \widehat \gamma_{N,h}, h = 0,\dots,H)$ given in (equation eq:gammars of the paper), where we consider $\widehat \gamma_{N,h}$ as an element of $\operatorname{HS}(L^2(\mathbb{Y}))$ for all $h$, with a slight abuse of notation. Suppose $\operatornamewithlimits{ess\text{ }sup}_{s \in \mathbb Y} d(s) < \frac{1}{4}$ and
\begin{equation} 
  \operatorname{E} \| \varepsilon_{0} \|^4_{L^2(\mathbb{Y})} < \infty. 
\end{equation}
Then, 
    \begin{equation}
        \sqrt{N} \begin{pmatrix}
            \widehat \gamma_{N,0} - \gamma_{0} \\
            \vdots \\
            \widehat \gamma_{N,H} - \gamma_{H}
        \end{pmatrix} \xrightarrow{d} 
        G \doteq
        \begin{pmatrix}
            G_0 \\
            \vdots \\
            G_H
        \end{pmatrix} \in \left(\operatorname{HS}(L^2(\mathbb{Y})\right)^{\times (H+1)},
    \end{equation}
    where the convergence holds in the topology of $(\operatorname{HS}(L^2(\mathbb{Y})))^{\times (H+1)}$, $G$ is a centered Gaussian element,
     and the covariance operator of $G$ is the operator $\Sigma$ given in (equation eq:Sigma of the paper)--(equation def:def:Aq-C of the paper), for $p,q=0,\dots, H$, and with $\mathbb{H}$ replaced by $L^2(\mathbb Y)$.

