[Lemma 7 (Analytic evaluation lemma) of arXiv:2607.26377, '\textbf{Entire Logarithmic Signatures\\ of Bounded-Variation Paths in Finite Dimensions}'] Let $\gamma:[0,T]\to V$ be continuous and of bounded variation, and put $g=S(\gamma)$ and $l=\log g$.
Assume $R(l)=\infty$.
Define
\[
A_{\Phi}(z)=\sum_{n\geq 1}z^n\Phi^{(n)}(l_n),
\qquad
G_{\Phi}(z)=\sum_{n\geq 0}z^n\Phi^{(n)}(S_n(\gamma)).
\]
Then both functions are entire and
\begin{equation}
G_{\Phi}(z)=\e^{A_{\Phi}(z)}
\qquad (z\in\C).
\end{equation}
Moreover,
\begin{equation}
\norm{G_{\Phi}(z)}
 \leq \exp\!\bigl(\abs{z}\,\norm{\Phi}\,L(\gamma)\bigr).
\end{equation}

