[Prop 55 of arXiv:2510.23423, 'One-arm exponents of the high-dimensional Ising model'] Let $d>4$. There exists $c>0$ such that, for every $n\geq 1$,
\begin{equation}
	\mathbf P^{\emptyset,\emptyset}_{\beta_c}[0\connect{\n_1+\n_2\:}\partial \Lambda_n]\geq \frac{c}{n^{d-2}}.
\end{equation}

