[Lemma of arXiv:2411.10296, 'Parking on a random rooted binary tree'] Let $\alpha > 2 - \sqrt{2}$. Then there exists $t \in (0,1)$ such that





    \begin{align*}
        G(s) &= p + s(1-p) + 2s^2 e^{\alpha (1-s)} \\
        &+ \begin{cases} 
         2s e^{\alpha (1-s)} \sqrt{s^2 - e^{\alpha (s-1)} (p + s(1+p))}, & 0 \leq s \leq t \\
        - 2s e^{\alpha (1-s)} \sqrt{s^2 - e^{\alpha (s-1)} (p + s(1+p))}, & t < s \leq 1
        \end{cases}
    \end{align*}

