[Lemma empirical-balancing of arXiv:2609.03858, 'High-Dimensional Learning Dynamics of \\ Attention-Indexed Models'] Fix \(T>0\), and let $N_T:=\left\lfloor\frac{Td}{\alpha_d}\right\rfloor$.
Let \(J\) be any stopping time such that, on \(\{n<J\}\),
\begin{equation}
\max_{1\le k\le K}\left\{\|U_k^{(n)}\|_{\mathrm{op}},\|V_k^{(n)}\|_{\mathrm{op}}\right\}\le C_*,
\qquad\|m^{(n)}\|_\infty\le R_*

\end{equation}
for some constants \(C_*,R_*<\infty\) independent of \(d,T,\gamma\). Under the conditions of Theorem (theo:untied-SGD of the paper), there exists \(c_D>0\), independent of \(d\), such that
\begin{equation}
\lim_{d\to\infty}\mathbb P\left(\inf_{\substack{0\le n<N_T\wedge J\\k\in\mathcal K}}\left(t_k^{A,(n)}+t_k^{B,(n)}\right)
\ge c_D\right)=1.

\end{equation}

