[Lemma 13 (Matrix exponential II) of arXiv:2604.02129, 'Realisation of constraints in underdamped Langevin dynamics'] Let $K \coloneqq \begin{pmatrix}
        0 & I \\ -\alpha I & - \gamma I 
    \end{pmatrix} \in \R^{2(d-k) \times 2(d-k)}$ with $\alpha,\gamma>0$, and $\theta= \sqrt{\gamma^2 - 4\alpha}$. Then for any $t\geq 0$
    \begin{align*}
        \bigl\|e^{Kt}\bigr\|^2_F \leq C (d-k) e^{-\eta t}, \text{ where } \eta \in (0,\gamma]\,, \  \eta = \begin{cases}
        \gamma - \sqrt{\gamma^2 - 4\alpha}, &\text{ if } \gamma^2 > 4\alpha \\ \gamma , &\text{ if } \gamma^2 < 4\alpha \\ \gamma - \delta , \text{ for any } \delta \in (0,\gamma) &\text{ if } \gamma^2 = 4\alpha .\end{cases} 
    \end{align*}

