[Definition Splitting distribution of arXiv:2605.22803, 'Persistence of asymptotic variance under transport:\\ from hyperfluctuation to stealthy hy'] Let $\cK^d_1:=\{B\in\cB^d: B \textnormal{ convex}, \lambda_d(B)=1\}$ and 
    \begin{equation}
        \cF^d_1:=\{(\phi,\tau): (\phi,\tau) \textnormal{ is a fair partition of } \R^d, C(x)\in\cK^d_1 \text{ for } x\in\phi\}.
    \end{equation}
    Suppose that $F$ is a probability kernel from $\cK^d_1$ to $\partial B_1$ which is only shape dependent, i.e.,
    \begin{equation}
        F(B+x) = F(B),\quad B\in\cK^d_1, x\in\R^d.
    \end{equation}
    Then $F$ is called a \textit{splitting distribution}.

