body:
[Satz thm:sufficiency-log of arXiv:2411.18155, 'Besov regularity of random wavelet series'] Let $d,k\in\mathds{N}$, $s,\alpha,\beta,\gamma,\theta\in\mathds{R}$, and $p,q\in (0,\infty]$.
Assume that $a$ follows a Besov sequence prior and $f$ follows a Besov prior, both with parameters $(\alpha,\beta,\gamma,\theta,k)$ and template random variable $X$, satisfying
\begin{equation}
\begin{cases} \:\exists\: \eps>0:\,\mathds{E}\bigl[\left\lvertX\right\rvert^p \cdot \log_2^+(\left\lvertX\right\rvert)\bigr]< \infty&\text{if }p\in (0,\infty),\\
\:\exists\:  R>0:\, \left\lvertX\right\rvert\stackrel{a.s.}{\leq}R&\text{if }p=\infty.\end{cases}
\end{equation}
If Property A holds, then $a$ almost surely belongs to $b^s_{p,q}(\mathds{R}^d)$.
Moreover, if Properties A and B are satisfied, then $f$ belongs almost surely to $B^s_{p,q}(\mathds{R}^d)$.

