[Lemma nonexplosition of arXiv:2411.01731, '$L^2$-Wasserstein contraction of modified Euler schemes for SDEs with high diffusivity and'] Under $({\bf H}_0)$  and $({\bf A}_1)$, it holds that for any $\delta\in(0,1]$, $x\in\mathds R^d,$ and $n\ge0,$
\begin{align}
\mathbb E|X_{n\delta}^{\delta,x}|^2\le\bigg(|x|^2+\frac{2c_*(1+c_*)+\sigma^2d}{2c^*(1+ c^*)}\bigg)\text{\rm{e}}^{2c^*(1+ c^*)n \delta}.
\end{align}

