{"artifact_digest":"sha256:b09f6df6141fbf539f9f8876e66b456dc41314f394d4b40fbeaee4ab94f9c647","artifact_path":"objects/sha256/b0/b09f6df6141fbf539f9f8876e66b456dc41314f394d4b40fbeaee4ab94f9c647.md","bundle_digest":"sha256:97e28ce81b41c16a34bdf446577a283657aa47381dbfd51169d8eb6e10754ee0","bundle_entry_key":"2608-25706-lemma-23-trace-norm-and-bures-wasserste","bundle_id":"population.tex-extract-s3_108","claim_kind":"lemma","conditions":[],"domain":"probability theory","draft":"tex-extract-20260907/bundle_s3_108.json","evidence_ids":[],"logical_id":"math:harvest.arxiv.mathematics:arxiv-2608-25706-lemma-23-trace-norm-and-bures-wasserste","overlay_schema_version":1,"proof_text":"Paper's own proof, opening: Use the Hilbert--Schmidt representation $\sd_{\rm BW}(A,B)=\inf_U\norm{A^{1/2}-B^{1/2}U}_{\rm HS}$. For $X=A^{1/2}$ and $Y=B^{1/2}U$, $A-B=(X-Y)X^\ast+Y(X^\ast-Y^\ast)$. By the H\"older inequality for the Schatten norm gives
    \begin{align*}
    \norm{A-B}_1
    \le\{\norm{X}_{\rm HS}+\norm{Y}_{\rm HS}\}
