Since a word of weight $k$ corresponds to a composition of $k$ with all parts at least $2$, there are only finitely many words of a fixed weight, and the bases $\{z_2^mv\}$ and $\{v\ast z_2^{\ast m}\}$ are therefore related by an invertible triangular matrix. This proves the existence and uniqueness in","release_manifest_digest":"sha256:5f107f74a6e79a1c9eb5b67c69c97a2bf4a6fc23941cd545198bcfc2cf69ae68","revision_digest":"sha256:df7c5e447c70dda3f3c18fe860549b492be55c968b79000cedb919fa253ff05a","source_id":"arxiv:2609.03777","source_revision":"tex-as-downloaded-2026-09-07","statement_fidelity_reviewed":false,"supersedes":[],"trust_class":"curated_secondary","truth_status":"unverified"}

body:
[Lemma le:beta-quotient-regimes of arXiv:2608.30382, 'Convergence rates for the RMSprop optimizer with full control of the hyperparameters'] Let $ n \in {\mathbb N} $, $ \beta \in [0,1) $.
Then one has that
\bas{
\frac{1-\beta}{1-\beta^n}\le \begin{cases} \frac{2}{n}, & \text{ if } n\le (1-\beta)^{-1}\\
\frac{1-\beta}{1-e^{-1}}, & \text{ if } n\ge (1-\beta)^{-1}
\end{cases}
}

