[Proposition phiE1 of arXiv:2606.24304, 'Quantitative Homogenization of PDEs with Neumann boundary conditions: a probabilistic appr'] Divide $[t,T]$ into subintervals with the same length $\Lambda>0$.  For any $q>1$,
\begin{eqnarray}  
{\mathbbm E}\left[\max_k\left(\phi^{t,x}_{(k+1)\Lambda}
-\phi^{t,x}_{k\Lambda}\right)^{2q}\right]\leqslant C\Lambda^{q-1}, 
\quad \sup_{\varepsilon >0}{\mathbbm E}\left[\max_k\left(\phi^{\varepsilon,t,x,y}_{(k+1)\Lambda}
-\phi^{\varepsilon,t,x,y}_{k\Lambda}\right)^{2q}\right]\leqslant C\Lambda^{q-1}.
\end{eqnarray}

