[Lemma lem:DEL of arXiv:2606.08325, 'Digit Mixing under Polynomial Maps'] Let \((Y_n)_{n\ge0}\) be complex random variables with \(|Y_n|\le1\), and consider the partial sums $S_N :=\sum_{n=0}^{N-1}Y_n$.
			If
			\begin{equation}
			\sum_{N=2}^{\infty}\frac{1}{N^3}\mathbb E|S_N|^2<\infty,
			\end{equation}
			then $ \frac{S_N}{N}\longrightarrow 0$ almost surely.

