[Cor no_individual_bubble_long of arXiv:2604.14122, 'The scaling limit of random walk and\\ the intrinsic metric on planar critical percolation'] There exist $\beta>0$, $\varepsilon>0$ such that the following holds for all $R$ sufficiently large and $p$ sufficiently small depending on $R$. For all $\alpha>\frac{3}{4}-\varepsilon$ for which~(equation eq:assumptionsubpoly of the paper) holds, we also have that for all $k$ and $n>R^k$,

\begin{equation}
    \begin{split}
        \mathbf{P}\!\left(\exists i\colon X_{x_{i},x_{i+1}}\geq \mathbf{q}_n\right)\leq C(R,\alpha)\cdot R^{-(\alpha+\beta)k},
    \end{split}
\end{equation} for some constant $C(R,\alpha)>0$.

