[Definition 8 of arXiv:2609.03736, '2609.03736'] For $A\in\mathcal H_E$, define the multiplication-by-$t$ map
$\mathsf S_t:\mathcal H_E\to\mathcal H_E$ by
\begin{equation}
 K_{\mathsf S_t(A)}(x,y)=t(x,y)K_A(x,y).

\end{equation}
The right side is again an invariant bundle kernel.  On the
$\Omega$-isotypic summand, the induced map is
\begin{equation}
 \Theta_\Omega(A)=z_\Omega\mathsf S_t(A)z_\Omega.

\end{equation}

