[Corollary 12 (Jiang--Lee--Vempala conjecture) of arXiv:2608.27657, '\bfseries Stein Kernels and Normal Approximation\\ for Log-Concave Bilinear Forms'] Assume the estimates in \cref{thm:letwin}.  If \(X,Y\in\R^n\) are
independent isotropic log-concave random vectors and \(G\sim N(0,1)\), then
\begin{equation}
  \boxed{
  W_2^2\!\left(
    \Law\!\left(\frac{\langle X,Y\rangle}{\sqrt n}\right),
    \Law(G)
  \right)
  \leq\frac{20}{n}.}
  \tag{5.12}
\end{equation}
Equivalently, if \(G_n\sim N(0,n)\), then
\begin{equation}
  W_2^2\!\left(\Law(\langle X,Y\rangle),\Law(G_n)\right)\leq20.
  \tag{5.13}
\end{equation}
Thus the dimension-free central limit conjecture of
Jiang, Lee, and Vempala \cite{JLV} follows from the cited estimates.

