body:
[Lemma quasimorphism of arXiv:2605.02226, 'Finitely Dependent Processes on Subshifts'] If $ (b_v)_{v \in \mathbb{Z}^d}$ is such that $ b_v \in \mathbb{Z}$, $b_\mathbf{0}=0$ and there exists a homomorphism $ \phi :\mathbb{Z}^d \rightarrow \mathbb{Z}$ and $ K < \frac{1}{4}\min\{|\phi(e_i)|: \phi(e_i) \neq 0\}$ such that       
    \begin{equation}
    |(|b_v - b_w| - |\phi(v-w)|)| \leq K \end{equation} 
    for every $ v, w \in \mathbb{Z}^d$. Then, there exists $ \epsilon_{i} \in \{ -1, 1\}$ such that the homomorphism 
    \[ \theta(v_1, v_2, \cdots, v_d) := \sum _{i=1}^{d}{\epsilon_i} \phi(v_i e_i)\]
    satisfies $ |b_v -\theta(v)| \leq 2Kd$ for all $ v \in \mathbb{Z}^d$.

