[Lemma lem:ldsde-coming-down of arXiv:2411.01364, 'Global Dynamics of Granular Media Equations via Stochastic Order'] Suppose Assumption (asp:potential of the paper) holds.
If $\mu\in C([0,\8);\mathcal P_2(\mathbb R))$, and if $\xi\in L^2(\Omega,\mathcal F_0,\mathbf P)$, then for any $p\geq2$, there exists a constant $C(p)=C(p,\alpha,\beta,\delta,\overline{\sigma}, \kappa, \theta,L)>0$ such that the unique solution $\{X_t^{\mu,\xi}\}_{t\geq0}$ of (equation eq:extrinsic-law-sde of the paper) satisfies
\begin{equation*}
\big(\mathbf E\big[|X_t^{\mu,\xi}|^p\big]\big)^{1/p}\leq
C(p)\Big(t^{-\frac{1}{\delta}}+t^{\frac{\kappa}{2}}+\sup_{s\in[0,t]}\|\mu_s\|_2^{\frac{2}{2+\delta}}\Big)\ \text{ for all $t>0$}.
\end{equation*}

