[Lemma lem:HSEP-seed-linear of arXiv:2608.02772, 'Non-Abelian Hirota-Miwa Equations for the KPZ Universality Class'] The seed functions $\Psi$ and $\Phi$ satisfy the linear
problem (equation eq:Linear-Psi-3 of the paper) and adjoint linear
problem (equation eq:Linear-Phi-Prob of the paper) on $\mathcal{V}$
with edge weights $(C_k, \Lambda_k)$.  Explicitly, for
$k \in \{1, 2\}$:
\begin{equation}
\Psi(S_k u) = \Psi(Tu) C_k - \Psi(u) \Lambda_k,
\end{equation}
and
\begin{equation}
\Phi(Tu) = C_k \Phi(S_k u) - \Lambda_k \Phi(T S_k u).
\end{equation}

[Definition def:overlap of arXiv:2602.12595, '\textbf{Michel Talagrand and the Rigorous Theory of Mean Field Spin Glasses}'] For independent replicas \(\sigma^1,\sigma^2\sim G_N\),
\begin{equation}
R_{1,2}=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^N \sigma_i^1\sigma_i^2\in[-1,1].
\end{equation}
For \(s\) replicas, define the overlap array \(\big(R_{\ell,\ell'}\big)_{1\le \ell<\ell'\le s}\).

