[Theorem thm:hopf-square of arXiv:2606.28869, '\bfseries A General Theory of Paths:\\ \large Signatures, Jump Lifts, and Expected Signatu'] With $X$ as in (prop:ito-sums of the paper) and $\mathrm{Sig}^M(X)=\mathrm{Sig}(X^{\mathrm{PL}})$ the signature of its chord interpolation, equivalently the Marcus lift,
\begin{equation}
\mathrm{Sig}^M(X)=\Phi\big(\mathrm{Sig}^I(X)\big).
\end{equation}
Equivalently, $\mathrm{Sig}^M$ is a shuffle character and the square
\begin{equation}
\begin{array}{ccc}
(z_1,\ldots,z_n) & \xrightarrow{\ \mathrm{iterated\ sums}\ } & \mathrm{Sig}^I\quad(\mathrm{quasi\mbox{-}shuffle})\\[1.5mm]
\big\downarrow{\scriptstyle\mathrm{chord\ fill}} & & \big\downarrow{\scriptstyle\Phi}\\[1.5mm]
X^{\mathrm{PL}} & \xrightarrow{\ \mathrm{iterated\ integrals}\ } & \mathrm{Sig}^M\quad(\mathrm{shuffle})
\end{array}

\end{equation}
commutes.

