body:
[Satz 1 of arXiv:2506.13661, 'Box-Covariances of Hyperuniform Point Processes'] Let $\eta$ be a stationary hyperuniform point process with box-symmetric truncated pair correlation measure $\beta$ satisfying $\int|y||\beta|(\mathrm{d} y)<\infty$. Then, 
	\begin{align}
		\mathrm{cov}(z)=\begin{cases}-\frac 1 {2d}\lambda_{d-1}(\partial \Lambda_1\cap \partial \Lambda_1(z)),\quad &\text{if } \mathring\Lambda_1\cap \mathring\Lambda_1(z)=\emptyset,\\
			\frac 1 {2d}\lambda_{d-1}(\partial \Lambda_1\cap \partial \Lambda_1(z)),\quad &\text{if }\mathring\Lambda_1\cap \mathring\Lambda_1(z)\neq\emptyset,
		\end{cases}
	\end{align}
	where $\partial \Lambda_1(z)$ is the boundary of $\Lambda_1(z)$ and $\mathring\Lambda_1(z)$ is the interior of $\Lambda_1(z)$. In particular, $\mathrm{cov}(z)$ is zero if the boxes are disjoint or if $z\in\mathring \Lambda_1$, it is 1 if $z=0$, and it is $- 1/ {(2d)}$ if $z\in\mathbb{Z}^d,|z|=1$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Corollary coro:m(t)-polynomial-time-not-going-out of arXiv:2604.20008, 'Mixing times of Langevin dynamics for \\ spiked matrix models'] Let $X_t$ be initialized at any point with $|m(X_0)|\geq \mathsf{m}_{3}$, and define the escape time below $\mathsf{m}_{2}$ as 
    $\tau^{\mathsf{out}}=\inf\{t>0 \ : \,|m_t|<\mathsf{m}_{2}\}$. For any time $T$ we have:  
    \begin{align*}
        \mathbb P[\tau^{\mathsf{out}} \leq T] \leq C T \exp(-cN) \, . 
    \end{align*}
    for $C,c>0$ constants independent of $N$ and $T$, depending only on $\beta$ and $\theta$.

