body:
[Proposition of arXiv:2608.10415, 'Continuous random variables'] For an element $a\in A$, the following are equivalent:
\begin{enumerate}
\item $a$ is positive, in the sense that $\sigma(a)\subset[0,\infty)$.

\item $a=b^2$, for some $b\in A$ satisfying $b=b^*$.

\item $a=cc^*$, for some $c\in A$.
\end{enumerate}

