body:
[Proposition 94 of arXiv:2605.10150, 'Rough path theory and an introduction to rough partial differential equations'] The convolution operator
\begin{align*}
\mathscr{I} : \big( C([0,T],D(A)), \| \cdot \|_{\infty} \big) \to \big( \scrd_X^{2\alpha}([0,T],W), \interleave \cdot \interleave_{X,2\alpha} \big)
\end{align*}
given by
\begin{align*}
Y \mapsto \bigg( \int_0^{\cdot} S_{\cdot - s} Y_s \, ds, 0 \bigg)
\end{align*}
is a continuous linear operator between Banach spaces with operator norm bounded by
\begin{align*}
\| \mathscr{I} \| \leq M e^{\omega T} (1+T) T^{1-2\alpha}.
\end{align*}

