{\mathbb P}(\bar\tau\ge n,\sigma^{(i)}> n)
&\le {\mathbb P}\Bigl(\bar\tau\ge n, v_n^{(i)}\le \frac {1-e^{-1/2}}{2} c\Bigr)\\
&\le {\mathbb P}\Bigl(\bar\tau\ge n, v_n^{(i)}\le \frac c2\Bigr)\le \exp\Bigl(-\frac q2\,\frac{1-\beta^n}{1-\beta}\Bigr).
}
For $n=1$, this already implies the claim. Thus we may assume that $n\ge2$. Since
\bas{
\frac{1-\beta^n}{1-\beta}=\sum_{k=0}^{n-1}\beta^k\ge n\beta^{n-1},
}
and since $n\le (1-\beta)^{-1}$ implies $\beta\ge 1-\frac1n$, we get for ...","release_manifest_digest":"sha256:5ff183d3d3ca192609bffed8dd25d7e96daca8bdbb0012add5e8a8241b37d1d4","revision_digest":"sha256:e797778c60a34d0c928743fe92042b1b46551613e98080bb55ac26b790945313","source_id":"arxiv:2608.30382","source_revision":"tex-as-downloaded-2026-09-08","statement_fidelity_reviewed":false,"supersedes":[],"trust_class":"curated_secondary","truth_status":"unverified"}

