	\begin{equation}
		\widetilde{P}(C)=P'(\textbf{Y}^{-1}(C)) \text{ for any }C\in\sigma(\mathcal{C}).
	\end{equation}

[Proposition prop:stima_HS_1 of arXiv:2605.07832, 'A Bismut -Elworthy formula for BSDEs with degenerate noise'] Assume that there exists a positive constant $\delta$ such that 
\begin{align}

\mu_n\sim  n^{\delta}, \qquad \delta>\frac{1}{\alpha}.
\end{align}
